window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Prologue","paragraphs":["In a bedroom which was not too big or too small, no light was on. The only thing that brightened the dark room was the computer screen.","On the desk, the computer was on, and in front of it sat a young man around 20 years old. Black messy hair. The same color eyes. All his focus was on the screen.","Yawn~","\"What time is it?\" he asked himself. He checked the time on his mobile, which lay just beside the keyboard.","When he double-tapped on the screen of the mobile, the screen lit up and showed the lock screen.","\"It’s 1:24 am,\" he muttered while looking at the time.","Why was he awake so late at night? Nothing much, just the usual. He read some web novels for a while, then watched some series, and then started to play games on his computer. It was like his every-night routine.","Currently, he was waiting for the new game to be downloaded.","Yeah, a new game. He was really excited to play this one. The game was new and had launched just a few weeks ago. But he didn’t bother to try it.","It’s not that he didn’t want to. But he was quite busy with his university. Well, less focus on university. Rather more focus on spending time with his friends.","Aron was not much of an outgoing person. He preferred to be at home and spend his time comfortably on comics, anime, and web novels. Sometimes games.","But what could he do? His friends, being too stubborn, dragged him outside. So he occasionally enjoyed their company as well. But they were all one hell of bastards.","Every time he went out with his friends, they always tried to—no... not tried to but they always did it. They insulted each other. Oddly, Aron liked that. It was really fun to tease each other. So, it would be a lie to say that he didn’t like going outside with friends.","It’s really good to go outside from time to time rather than staying at home all day. But again, he also liked to stay at home while reading and playing games.","Beep!","Beep!","Just then Aron’s computer made a sound, informing him that the game was downloaded and it was ready to be played.","\"Finally!\" He was excited to play this game.","Aron straightened in his chair, fatigue momentarily forgotten. The loading bar had vanished, replaced by a sleek black icon etched with golden letters. The sleep that had come to him vanished instantly.","Odyssey of Eternal Gods’ War","Just the name alone sounded heavy. Like the kind of game that involved gods dying, worlds burning, and heroes screaming their last breath in glorious slow motion.","The game did have an academy for the starting part of the story. Major events would occur in that academy. Later, the story would be focused on outside of the academy in future updates.","At least that much information Aron had learned from the internet.","He cracked his knuckles. \"Well... let’s see what all the hype is about.\"","Aron wasn’t a hardcore gamer by any means. He didn’t grind rankings, didn’t chase leaderboards, and definitely didn’t spend money on skins. Games, for him, were just another way to relax. Like web novels, anime, or binge-watching a series at 3 a.m. when he definitely shouldn’t be awake.","But now it had become a habit of his.","The screen went black.","Then.","Boom!","A low, ancient horn echoed through his headphones.","The darkness split apart, revealing a ruined battlefield drenched in blood. Broken banners fluttered in the wind. Corpses, both human and monstrous, littered the land. The sky itself seemed cracked, crimson lightning crawling through dark clouds.","Space shattered around by an unknown force.","Aron blinked.","\"...Damn.\"","A deep, almost divine voice resounded.","> When gods wage war, mortals become ashes","\"The graphics are peak!\" he exclaimed joyfully.","The cinematic unfolded like a movie. Armies clashed. Dragons fell from the sky. A radiant figure was pierced by a black spear, their light shattering like glass. Somewhere in the chaos, a lone silhouette stood atop a mountain of corpses, gazing at the heavens with cold, defiant eyes.","Goosebumps rose on Noah’s arms.","\"Okay,\" he muttered, leaning closer. \"This is actually kinda sick.\"","The scene faded.","[Welcome to Odyssey Of Eternal Gods’ War]","A lobby appeared first.","There was a gallery option, having a list of important characters of the story.","He clicked on it before starting the first playthrough.","Dozens of names scrolled down the screen, each accompanied by a small portrait and a title.","> Damien Ashworth","> Lyria Sunweave","> Kaelan Nightfall",".",".",".","....","Aron scrolled lazily, not really reading in detail. He wasn’t planning to start seriously tonight anyway. It was already late, and his eyelids were getting heavier by the second.","They had given the main character and side characters list here. Their information was written here. Aron scrolled it while reading them lazily.","Still, one name made his finger pause.","> Noah Eldritch – ???","\"...Huh?\"","That name caught his attention.","The portrait belonged to a very handsome young man. Maybe the most handsome male character till now. Even more than the protagonist. The title slot was empty. There was no description about him. No powers or information. No, there was actually one piece of information in the description. A single word.","\"Extra? That’s... weird. Why would they have a character image of an extra? Is it because he has some small but important role?\"","Maybe it was the default name? Or some placeholder character? He shrugged. New games always had bugs.","Before he could click anything else, another window popped up.","[Prologue: The Beginning of the End]","[Start Cinematic?]","He hesitated, then clicked Yes.","The screen dimmed once more.","This time, the view shifted to a grand city of white stone and towering spires. People walked the streets, laughing, trading, and living peacefully. Completely unaware of the shadow creeping toward them.","A young man stood on a balcony, staring at the sky.","> Fate is a cruel thing","The narrator said softly.","> Especially for those who do not know they stand at its center","The boy turned. For a split second, his face was clear.","Aron’s breath hitched.","\"...He’s a pretty handsome guy.\"","The boy had short black hair. A pair of striking gold-colored eyes.","He was the protagonist of this game. The playable character.","The young man’s lips curved slightly, as if smiling directly at Aron.","’What?!’","Before he could process that thought, his vision blurred. The cinematic cut abruptly, replaced by the game’s main menu again.","[Servers Online]","[Enter World]","Aron stared at the screen for a few seconds, then yawned hard, rubbing his eyes.","\"Okay... yeah. That’s enough for today.\"","He saved nothing. Selected nothing. Just closed the game.","Tomorrow, he told himself. ’I’ll actually play tomorrow.’","He shut down his computer, the room plunging into darkness. Crawling onto his bed, Aron didn’t even bother setting an alarm. His mind was already drifting, fragments of the cinematic replaying behind his eyelids.","Yawn~","’I will play it properly tomorrow night.’","Gods, war. Those characters. He started to think about them. He had read all the characters’ information so he wouldn’t have any problems later on. While thinking such things, sleep slowly took him instantly.","The thought barely finished before slumber claimed him.","This would be the last time he would sleep in his room.","Then something began to feel wrong.","A faint, unfamiliar scent reached his nose. Metallic. It was a sharp smell like blood.","Aron’s brows knit together. His body felt heavy, unmoving, as if he were sinking into something cold and endless. The darkness behind his eyelids shifted, no longer peaceful or empty.","Then pain exploded through him. It was scorching, violent, and all-encompassing.","It tore through his limbs, his chest, his very core, like his body was being ripped apart and reforged at the same time. His breath caught in his throat, but no sound came out.","His senses screamed.","This wasn’t a dream.","Then slowly he forced himself to open his heavy eyelids.","Only to find himself in an entirely different place."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Waking Up In Unknown Place","paragraphs":["An unknown forest lay shrouded in silence, broken only by the thick stench of blood saturating the air.","In one shadowed clearing, five human bodies were strewn across the forest floor. Their forms were twisted and broken, clothes torn and soaked in dark, drying crimson.","Deep wounds carved into flesh told a violent story. One that had ended moments ago. Limbs lay limp and lifeless, eyes staring blankly into nothingness, as if frozen in their final moments of terror.","But a little distance away from them lay another human body. He was alive. His chest rose and fell as he breathed.","He was a young man around his twenties. His hair was messy and snow-white in color– smooth, soft, and silky. His skin was fair, and he had an extremely handsome face. His eyes were closed.","After a few seconds, his eyelids started fluttering open. A pair of beautiful crystal-blue eyes tried to see what was in front of him. His crystal-blue eyes struggled to understand what was happening as blurred shapes filled his vision.","Slowly, the haze faded. A clear blue sky came into view, along with tree branches overhead, their leaves gently fluttering in the breeze.","’Where am I?’ A sudden pain shot through his body.","\"Gah—!\" he groaned in pain.","He tried to push himself up. Using his hands for support, he managed to sit upright.","There was a cut on his chest. His grey-colored leather outfit was torn. Warm blood was still streaming down. His face had several scratches. Wounds covered his body.","A scorching pain ran through him.","’What’s this?!’ he thought in confusion, seeing the fresh blood streaming down from his chest. The deep cut carved across it.","Thump!","Thump!","Thump!","His heart started to beat faster. Fear crawled over his back.","\"I am hurt–!\"","Munch!","Munch!","Munch!","Before he could think more about his situation, a munching sound attracted his attention. His head turned to his right.","’What?!’","His eyes widened in shock.Multiple dead human bodies lay there, lifeless and bloodied.","Near them stood a huge bear.","No, it was not any normal bear he had seen on a mobile screen or TV. It was far bigger than any ordinary bear. A huge horn erupted from its forehead. Its fur was dark black in color. Its eyes glowed red.","It was eating one of the dead bodies. Tearing it apart, digging its massive jaw into the stomach and devouring the flesh.","\"Keck—!\"","Seeing that scene, the young man felt like vomiting. He covered his mouth with his right palm.","But the sound was louder than his muttering.","The monster stopped chewing on its human meal. Its head snapped toward the source of the sound. Its glowing red eyes locked onto the human who was still alive.","GROWLLL!","It growled loudly upon seeing the living human. The man’s eyes widened. A primal chill ran down his spine.","’Shit!’","His body was injured, wracked with pain. Yet at this moment, the pain didn’t matter. The monster growled at him. It was ready to dash forward.","Just before that, he got up from the ground, spun on his feet, and started to run away from the bear monster in the opposite direction.","Stomp!","Stomp!","Stomp!","He ran through the forest, weaving past tall, twisted trees. He didn’t look behind. Just kept running.","While behind him.","ROAAARRRR!","The monster followed with fury, raging.","’Hah!... What’s happening? Where am I? How did I come here? Why is there a real monster here?’","The young man had been in his bedroom just a few hours ago. How had he ended up here, in such a dire situation?","The young man running was none other than Aron.","Thump!","Thump!","He had never seen such a thing before, unless it was in movies or games. But now, a real monster was chasing him.","Was he in some kind of dream?","\"Ahh!\" He groaned in pain. Every step sent agony through his body, making it clear that he was not dreaming.","’This can’t be a dream.’","He turned his head back. The monster was much closer now.","\"NO!\" He ran faster. Blood leaked from the corner of his mouth. His blue eyes focused straight ahead.","ROAAARR!","The monster was already close. It leapt over his head.","’No! No! I can’t die!’","He threw himself to the left.","BOOM!","The bear’s claws slammed into the ground where Aron had been moments ago. The impact cracked the earth.","Aron rolled across the ground multiple times, then struggled back to his feet.","\"Damn! This body!\" He cursed his injured body. It was really hard to move with this body.","He didn’t look back and ran in another direction. The monster didn’t let him escape. It chased him again, even more furious.","ROOOARRRR!","The bear monster was faster than before. It already catching up to him.","It swung its right arm and slammed it into Aron’s right rib cage.","Crack.","The sound of something breaking echoed.","\"Arggh!\"","The blow was so strong that the young man was thrown aside, crashing into a tree loudly.","Thud!","\"Aaarghh!\" he screamed in pain. The impact nearly knocked him unconscious. He struggled to stay focused.","His left hand clutched his rib cage where he had been struck.","’My bones... they’re broken inside.’ The realization chilled him. His head throbbed, veins bulging on his forehead.","He was losing blood as time passed. His breathing was ragged. He needed to do somthing. If not, he might die.","He sat there, back against the tree trunk, legs stretched out. With little strength to move.","What should he do? It was becoming hard to think straight. One cheek was swollen. His eyelids barely stayed open.","The monster looked at him.","Growl!","It growled while gazing at the half-dead body in front of it.","The monster opened its mouth wide. Its teeth were large and jagged. They were pointy shaped. They were meant to tear enemies or prey apart.","It brought its gaping mouth down to bite Aron, to end his life on the spot.","’I need to do something... I need to... I can’t.’ He thought weakly.","He pushed himself up. Fear of death, the last instinct. Surged through his body.","He moved before he could think.His right hand shot forward.","He didn’t know what he was doing, but it felt as if his body had done this countless times before.","Something warm circulated through him from his abdomen. It was unknown. Yet familiar, as if it were an essential part of him.","Something formed in front of his hand. The air trembled around his hand. Coldness spread outward near it. He felt it clearly. The chill, the coldness forming before his hand.","Out of nowhere, something like a blue crystal shape appeared. It was long, bigger than his fist, with a sharp, solid tip.","His hand was already inside the monster’s wide-open mouth.","Everything happened in just few seconds.","Aron’s half-closed eyes snapped open. He could guess it. What was forming in front of his extended hand.","’...Ice?’"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: Noah Eldritch (1)","paragraphs":["The young man stared at the ice crystal formed before his right hand. It sends cold sensation around his hand.","’....Ice?’","He was confused. But he felt as if this was not anything new. Something that was part of him..","He saw the monster near his hand.","’I need to shoot it!’","The moment he thought about countering the enemy. The blue color crystal shot forward.","Crush!","Splashed","Crimson blood splashed in air. This time it does not belong to Aron. The ice crystal shot inside the monster’s mouth. Dugged inside its upper side of mouth painfully.","Rooooooooaarrr!","The monster step back while screaming in pain. Still it didn’t fell on ground. It shook its head wildly. Mouth still wide open.","The crystal finally loosed and fell down from its mouth.","Grwolllll~","It growl, as blood leaked from its mouth. Then it looked at Aron’s side in pure hatred.","But there was no one sitting at tree.","He had already got up from that place. Aron had felt like he had a chance. He can do magic. How? He don’t know. But logic was not important here. The important right now was to use this mysterious power.","If there was a chance of survival then he had to do anything for it.","His brain started to think about manifesting a weapon. Something that he could held easily in his hand. Not too big or heavy. But it should be sharped. A weapon that can help him to cut his enemy.","He was running towards the monster from other side.","The same warm energy ran through his veins like blood. It gathered around his right hand as something cold started to form in his palm.","The ice started to take shaped. It slowly turned into a sharp dagger like weapon. The ice blade of that dagger was sharped. Like it was made up of real steel.","The bear monster saw him coming near. It swung its claw hand horizontally to shattered the head of the young man.","Aron’s body was battered. Pain all over his body yet it moved...it moved in desire for survival. To remained alive. Adrelined rushed. His heart pump faster.","’I need to avoid it!’ He bend down instantly. The muscular hand moved above its head. He could feel the breeze form by it.","His grip tightened on the ice daggers hilt.","He swung it at the stomach area.","Slash","The blade dug lightly on its fat and thick skin.","Then he used his left hand. Pushing his whole strength by both hands.","\"Ahh!\" Arond screamed. This time it was not a scream of pain. Rather it was because of pushing his all limits.","The blade dug deeper as Aron pushed forward, sliding it horizontally across the monster’s stomach. It cut deeper.","Slash!","A wet, tearing sound echoed.","The ice blade carved through thick flesh. Blood burst out, splashing onto the forest floor. The monster’s body trembled violently as the wound widened. It continued to leak blood.","ROOOOOAAARRRRR!!","A deafening scream of agony tore through the forest. It was more painful scream than before.","The bear monster reared back, roaring in pain. Its massive hand swung wildly and slammed into Aron’s body.","’Shitt!’","BOOM!","\"Gaahh!\"","The impact was brutal. Aron was sent flying again sideways, his body crashing violently into the ground.","Thud!","He rolled several times before coming to a stop. Pain exploded through his body. His vision blurred. The taste of blood filled his mouth.","\"Aghh—!\" he groaned weakly.","His body refused to move.","Meanwhile, the monster staggered back, blood pouring from the huge gash carved across its stomach. Flesh hung loosely, soaked in crimson. The wound was deep. Deep enough to expose muscle beneath.","For a brief moment, Aron thought he had succeeded in killing the monster. That cut might be enough to kill the monster","’Did I... kill it?’","But he was wrong. The monster did not fall. It was still standing.","It straightened slowly, breathing heavily. Blood dripped from its body, splashing onto the soil. Its glowing red eyes burned with madness and rage.","Growlll...","The monster was still alive. His stomach cut opened yet it remained alive. Standing there while glaring at him.","Aron’s heart sank. ’No! Why? That should be enough, isn’t it?’","His body lay sprawled on the ground, unmoving. His limbs felt numb. Breathing itself was painful.","The monster locked its gaze onto him.","Then—","Stomp","Stomp","Stomp","It began to charge.","Each step shook the ground as it dashed toward young man’s motionless body, intent on finishing him.","’I... can’t move...’ His face became incredibly pale because of his situation.","His consciousness wavered. Was this his end?","Just as the monster closed the distance.","A sudden flash of dark green light tore through the forest.","WHOOSH!","Something moved at blinding speed. Aron couldn’t see it clearly.","Before the monster could react, the green light passed straight through its body.","A clean green line drawn into the space.","For a split second, everything went silent.","After that,","Slice","The bear monster froze mid-step. Its eyes widened in horror.","A thin line appeared across its body.","The next moment, its massive form split cleanly in half.","Blood sprayed violently as the upper portion slid off and crashed onto the ground.","BOOM!","The lower half collapsed a heartbeat later.","The monster was dead. It was lifeless gruesome.","The forest fell silent once more.","Aron’s blurry vision barely caught the sight of a man standing where the green light had stopped.","He looked to be in his late twenties.","A sword rested in his hand, its blade faintly glowing. A cold, dense green aura flowed around his body like mist.","His posture was calm. He was composed.","His eyes sharp and cold emerald colour. They shifted towards Aron. The man had dark brown colour hair, faintly swaying in breeze.","Those eyes met his. Relief flooded Aron’s chest. He was a human.","’...I survived...finally’ Aron thought. His will powered to stay consciousness was slowly diminishing. He couldn’t think much. It was harder to think anything. Now he had to believe in the man who was in front of him.","That was his last option.","’Hope...he will sa-save me.’","The tension finally left his body.","His breathing became relaxed. Eyelids heavy with exhaustion.","The man observed the young man lying in front of him. He walked towards Aron and been down on his one knees.","\"You are Noah Eldritch...At least you are alive...\" The man guess it from his appearance. Snow white hair. Crystal blue color eyes.","Aron heard that name. The name sounds familiar to him.","’...Noah Eldritch?’","He heard that name before consciousness slipped away. Darkness claimed him once more."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Noah Eldritch (2)","paragraphs":["White walls reflected the soft glow of overhead lights. The air smelled faintly of medicines and herbs, but it was also mixed with a metallic scent.","A single large window stretched across one wall, rain tapping softly against the glass, the city skyline blurred beyond it.","The bed stood at the center, sheets tucked tight with practiced precision. Silver railings framed it, polished and cold. Beside it, a sleek monitoring unit hummed quietly, its screen pulsing with a soft blue light instead of the usual green.","On the bed lay a young man. His snow-white hair was soft and messy. His eyelashes and eyebrows had the same color as his hair.","He possessed an extremely handsome face. Bandages were wrapped around his body on the parts where he was hurt.","His chest rose and fell as he breathed calmly.","He had not been unconscious for very long. A sound suddenly echoed in his brain. It was something that could not be heard by anyone else but him.","The sound was getting louder and continuous. The young man’s face frowned. He shook his head slightly. His eyes twitched as he started to flutter open his eyelids. Blue, confused eyes stared upward, but it was not the white ceiling that came into his view.","A blue translucent screen was floating in front of him.","’What that?... A status window? System? Am I in another world or something like that?’ Being a gamer and a novel reader, he made some assumptions.","Now everything clicked for him. How he was in the forest. How there was a monster. And how he could even use magic.","’What world am I in?’ he thought gravely.","On the screen, something was going on, making loud sounds in his brain.","[Error!]","[Error!]","[Trying to synchronize with user....0%! 0%! 0%!]","[Failed!]","[The synchronization is failing]","[Failed]","[Merging memory of Noah Eldritch with user]","The moment he read that, a sharp pain passed through his brain.","\"Aargg!\" He groaned in pain, holding his head with both hands. Unknown memories started to enter him.","But the pain did not remain for long as it slowly subsided. The mechanical voice was still coming. He stared back at the screen, his eyes hazy. He blinked a few times to get a clear vision. Veins bulged on his head because of the pain that had just come to him.","[Succeed! Merging memory is completed. User will get memories of Noah Eldritch slowly, so he won’t feel too much strain on his brain.]","[Synchronize system with user]","[Error!]","[System cannot synchronize with user! The soul is not compatible!]","[Ding!]","[User doesn’t have any knowledge of future]","[Survival chances until the end.....0%!]","[Ding!~]","[System cannot be initiated. But for poor user who has no future... We pity you!]","[System cannot work with you. Still, to help you, we will give you something. For each event you survive, you will be rewarded according to your contribution in the scenario! That’s all we can do for you.]","Aron, who was now Noah. Widened his eyes. ’Wait, does that mean you won’t talk to me? Or help?’ he asked worriedly.","[...]","[Affirmative]","[We cannot talk with you. You will be automatically rewarded if you are involved in the storyline. In each scenario. If you are not involved, you won’t get anything.]","[Best of luck, use–no. Best of luck, Extra!]","[Now bye!]","[---]","---","Just like that, everything went silent. Finally, he felt peace in his mind.","Noah kept staring, this time at the white ceiling of the hospital room.","His brain still throbbed slightly.","’I am Noah Eldritch... from Odyssey of Eternal Gods’ War.’","He chuckled at his situation. How could this be possible? This situation was the worst way possible.","Just last night, he downloaded this game and read the character list, in which there was also a character named Noah. Known as an extra.","’Was this the reason why that character was on the list, despite being an extra? But why me? I haven’t even played the game. I have no knowledge. Why am I transmigrated?’","\"Hah,\" he exhaled tiredly, rubbing his temples. By some miracle, his body was not aching much. It was not very hard to move. It must be because of having magic in this world.","He could not find any reason. What impact could he have on a world where he had no future knowledge? Not having a system that could make him overpowered, what could he do here?","Sigh...","He decided to rest for a while. No need to push himself too much. He was still recovering.","’Did the original owner die in the forest... and then I transmigrated into his body?’","Despite trying his best to push these thoughts aside, he simply could not.","\"Damn... what about the original me? What about my family? Am I dead or what?\" he muttered in a low voice.","He closed his eyes for a moment. The thought of not being able to see them... not knowing for how long... started to make him sad.","His mother’s gentle voice echoed faintly in his memory. The way she always called him during dinner. The way she complained that he worked too much and slept too late.","His father’s quiet presence. The man rarely said much, but always left cut fruits on the table when Noah stayed up late working.","Noah worked hard in his previous life. As much as he stay up late night while playing games or watching series. He also used to study hard when it was needed. Studying for late night.","Not because he was ambitious, but because he wanted an easy and comfortable life. He also wanted to give his parents a comfortable life.","’Everything is gone just like that... in one single night... now I don’t even know if I can meet them ever.’ He clenched his fist tightly.","’I didn’t even get to say goodbye if I was going to come here.’","He had always believed transmigration stories were cool. But he never wished to experience one. He was really happy with his life.","He was not a loner. He didn’t have any sad past. He was not even bored with his life.","Then why did he transmigrate?","While thinking about those things, the door of the room slid open.","Noah’s eyes turned in the direction of the sound. There, the same man who had saved him was standing at the door.","\"Oh! You woke up.\" The man exclaimed with relived expression."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Noah Eldritch (3)","paragraphs":["The man stepped fully into the room, the door sliding shut softly behind him.","He looked to be in his late twenties. Short brown hair rested neatly atop his head.","His emerald-green eyes were calm and clear, carrying a quiet confidence. His expression was relaxed, neither overly friendly nor cold.","He was tall and well-built, his broad shoulders filling the doorway with ease. Even without armor or weapons, there was no mistaking it. This was a man who had fought many battles. The same man who had pulled Noah back from the edge of death in the forest.","He walked closer to the bed, his footsteps light against the polished floor.","\"So,\" he said, his voice steady and composed, \"how are you doing?\"","Noah blinked and slowly pushed himself into a sitting position, wincing slightly but managing it without much trouble.","\"I... I’m alive,\" Noah replied after a moment, his voice hoarse. \"So I guess that’s good.\"","The man gave a faint smile, clearly relieved.","\"That’s more than good,\" he said. \"You were in a bad state when I found you. I wasn’t sure you’d wake up this soon.\"","Noah studied him carefully. The calm demeanor, the lack of arrogance. It all felt oddly reassuring.","\"You saved me,\" Noah said quietly. \"In the forest.\"","The man nodded once, as if it were nothing worth mentioning.","\"I did what I needed to do,\" he replied. \"Rest easy. You’re safe here.\"","The word safe lingered in Noah’s mind longer than it should have.","He felt relieved. And yet, deep down, he knew this calm wouldn’t last forever.","\"But... I couldn’t save your companions. The one who was supposed to guide your group safely was able to send an emergency signal to me about being chased by a Rank C monster. It had just newly broken through to C rank. I am sorry for not being able to go and save everyone.\" His eyes dropped as he sigh.","Sigh","Noah did get some memories of this body. They were scattered, but he did remember how he had been in the forest.","He had come here with the intention to practice, killing monsters in the forest, learning how to do exploration. With the help of a guide given by the guild.","There were other young men with him. Just like him, they had also come for practice and to gain experience.","They were exploring an area where only weak and low-level monsters roamed. It was nearly impossible for a strong one to exist in that area.","But the worst thing happened. There was a high-ranking monster. It killed everyone... except Noah. Maybe Noah did die... and Aron took his place.","Noah just nodded while listening to the man in front of him.","\"Don’t apologize. It’s not your fault... also, thanks again. You still saved me in time,\" Noah said.","In truth, those other men were strangers. He didn’t know them. Their guide being a D-rank adventurer was enough for the exploration. No monster stronger than D-rank was supposed to be present in that area.","But it seemed their luck was not good.","The forest belonged to a mid-level guild named Ironfist. Noah had paid them for this to train here and get some experience.","He could remember that much.","The brown-haired man studied Noah for a while. \"You are different from what I heard.\"","Noah raised his eyes and looked at the man in confusion. \"What do you mean by different?\"","\"Noah Eldritch... exiled son of Duke Eldritch. You don’t have any vile or bad personality as the rumors say.\"","That information shocked Noah.","’What the heck? Son of Duke Eldritch. Exiled son! What in the name of the gods! This is the worst cliché possible now.’","Again, he didn’t receive the memories all at once. They were slowly coming, so he still didn’t have much idea about himself.","’So I was a retarded young master... who had done vile things... and in the end got exiled from his family. Damn! This is the worst thing possible.’ He thought bitterly.","Noah started to curse his situation while the brown-haired man continued to observe him.","Knowing that this man was still watching him, Noah replied, \"Well... I have changed a lot since getting exiled. Now I understand how wrong I was.\" He gave an awkward smile.","Without having much knowledge, Noah started to spout some nonsense.","\"Oh... I can understand that. Situations do change people, either for good or bad. It seems it had a good effect on you.\"","Noah didn’t respond and just nodded. He decided to change the subject. \"By the way, what’s your name? You saved me, yet I don’t even know your name, sir.\"","The man crossed his hands over his chest and chuckled. \"Haha. No need to call me sir. My name is Cedric Winston. You can just call me Cedric.\"","\"Okay. In that case, I’ll call you that. Thanks again, Cedric.\"","\"You should rest more. Your hospital bill will be paid by the guild. Also, you will get back your money for this training plan, and we will give you compensation as well.\"","Noah’s eyes lit up at that. \"I appreciate that.\"","\"We can only do that much for you, since you faced near death because of us. Okay, I’ll get going. See you later.\"","\"Yeah. See you.\"","Saying that, Cedric left Noah alone.","Once he was alone, Noah closed his eyes.","\"This is too much. It’s a more dire situation than I thought.\"","He did remember where he currently lived. He also had some money. It seemed his family didn’t seize his accounts or money.","The real problem now was what Noah had done till now. Because whatever disastrous things the previous Noah had done, now it was his responsibility to face them.","\"At least I’ll get some money and compensation. But why did I decide to take the exploration training plan... was I really someone who trained hard and wished to get stronger?\"","Noah rubbed his temples, trying to remember as much as possible.","Just then, his eyes widened.","’Academy! It’s starting soon! I was trying to get stronger and gain experience before the academy starts.’","Noah’s expression turned ugly. He was an exiled, notorious young master. Then there was the academy. He could already guess, this wouldn’t be easy for him. Despite having little knowledge, he had a few assumptions about his character’s role in the game.","Noah looked outside the window. It was raining.","’It’s raining outside of its season... since it’s early spring.’","He continued to stare outside while mocking his fate."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: New Home For Now","paragraphs":["Noah stood at the entrance of the hospital. He was discharged now after staying there for the whole day.","He was wearing a normal navy blue t-shirt and black trousers. His white hair was still messy. Yet he looked too handsome. His height was around 182 cm, nearly six feet tall, with a well-built physique.","Honestly, when Noah saw himself in the mirror that morning, he was baffled and happy. He was extremely handsome. So of course he was happy.","He also got his money back with extra compensation. He was delighted about that.","Noah started to walk through the streets of the city.","He was currently in a city named Crythos. He had been living in this same city for the last two months.","Noah stepped out onto the main street, the city unfolding before him in steel, glass, and light.","Towering skyscrapers stretched into the pale sky, their reflective surfaces catching the afternoon sun.","Digital billboards wrapped around entire buildings, flashing advertisements for mana-tech devices, core stabilizers, and the latest combat gear brands.","Cars moved in steady streams along wide roads, their engines humming softly. Some were entirely silent, powered by refined mana batteries.","Citizens filled the sidewalks. Office workers in tailored suits, young students in school uniforms, and street vendors selling steaming snacks from compact metal carts.","The air carried a mix of roasted coffee and fresh street food.","Holographic traffic signals flickered at intersections, adjusting automatically as crowds thickened.","Above the roads, there was a bridge. A metro train ran across it smoothly without making any sound.","Everything felt alive. Life was fast and efficient, just like his past world.","’It doesn’t feel much different from my world. The only thing different is that it’s a magical world... with a monarchy system, not a democracy.’","Beneath the modern polish, Noah could sense it. Mana flowing invisibly through the city like veins beneath skin. Security drones hovered lazily overhead, scanning for unstable cores or unauthorized spell use. Mana was the primary energy source here for everything.","A group of teenagers walked past him laughing, one casually forming a small orb of flame in his palm before snuffing it out with a grin.","In this world, magic wasn’t just imagination.","’I need to take a bus to go to my apartment.’","Noah reached the bus station and waited for the bus to come.","He checked the storage ring on his right hand’s index finger. ’It’s amazing to have such tech. I can carry many things without any problem.’","He was shocked, but not too much. Mostly because he was slowly getting memories from the real Noah.","Just then the bus arrived, and Noah climbed onto it with the other passengers. Many of them glanced at him, especially women.","Though most people here were very good-looking compared to his past world, Noah was especially more handsome and good-looking compared to many of them.","He paid for his ride on the machine beside the driver. His destination was Navor.","He took a seat near the window. The bus slowly started and ran through the clean roads. The city looked beautiful.","’Oh, I didn’t check my status.’","The movement he thought about status. A blue translucent screen appeared in front of him which was only visible to him.","===STATUS===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 years","Strength: 79","Speed: 67","Stamina: 84","Endurance: 61","Charm: 501","Mana: 640","Core Rank: Dormant (High)","Potential: Refined Core (High)","Profession: [Swordsmanship Lvl.1], [Spearmanship Lvl.1]","Technique: None","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind]","Innate Ability: Ice Creation","===","Noah observed his stats while folding his hands under his chest.","\"It’s okay, I guess,\" he muttered.","In truth, he was really disappointed with his stats. He was still at Dormant Core.","Which was the first level of core ranks. So he was at the bottom. At least he was at the high stage, indicating that he could soon break through to the Awakened rank.","In this world, everyone had mana inside their body since birth. But they did not gain true awareness of it immediately. They had to circulate it and try to form a core as they adapted and grew older.","Not everyone could form a mana core. But those who were able to form a Dormant Core could see a status window where their physical stats, abilities, and potential were visible.","At the Dormant level, a person could only do normal things and some low-level basic spells.","Normal-level body enhancement was very limited. Also, mana control was very hard. Sometimes it became unstable to use.","Noah was at the high stage of Dormant Core, which meant his control over mana was good.","Also, some people gained an innate ability once they formed a Dormant Core. It was rare; not everyone possessed an innate ability.","Noah was lucky to have one.","\"As much as I know from the memories... having an Awakened Core in the first year at the academy is very common. Being at the high stage is ideal.\"","He closed the status window.","Soon the bus came to a smooth halt at Navor Street.","The doors slid open with a soft hiss.","Noah stood up, adjusting his shirt slightly before stepping down onto the pavement. The bus pulled away almost immediately, merging back into the flow of traffic.","Navor Street was quieter compared to the main roads. The towering commercial buildings were replaced with mid-rise residential complexes.","Cafés with outdoor seating lined one side of the street, while convenience stores and small mana-device repair shops occupied the other.","He walked at a normal pace.","Streetlights stood evenly spaced along the sidewalks, their bases etched with faint rune lines that glowed softly as evening approached. The air here felt calmer and less rushed than the city center.","After a few minutes, Noah stopped in front of a twelve-story residential building.","Silvercrest Residences, Block C – 118 Navor Street, Crythos","The building’s exterior was simple but modern. Gray concrete layered with dark glass panels. A digital security panel stood beside the entrance.","Noah tapped the screen and pressed his thumb against the verification pad. A faint blue light scanned his fingerprint.","Resident Verified – Unit C-804","The doors slid open.","The lobby inside was modest but clean. Soft lighting illuminated marble-patterned tiles. A reception desk sat unattended at the side, replaced mostly by automated systems.","A pair of indoor plants stood near the elevator, their leaves unusually vibrant, likely enhanced by mana-infused soil.","Noah stepped into the elevator and pressed 8.","The ride was smooth and silent.","When the doors opened, a quiet hallway greeted him. Beige walls, evenly spaced doors, and muted lighting gave the place a calm atmosphere. His footsteps echoed faintly as he walked down the corridor.","He stopped in front of Unit C-804.","Pulling a small metallic keycard from his pocket, he tapped it against the lock. The door clicked open.","Noah stepped inside.","The apartment was not too big but comfortable, perfect for a single person.","A small living area greeted him first. A dark gray sofa faced a huge black TV screen.","A simple glass coffee table stood in front of it. To the right was a compact kitchen space. Clean counters, a two-burner induction stove, a small refrigerator, and neatly arranged cabinets.","To the left, a short hallway led to the bedroom and bathroom.","The bedroom held a queen-sized bed with plain white sheets, a study desk placed near the window, and a built-in wardrobe. The window overlooked the city skyline, now tinted orange as the sun began to lower.","It wasn’t luxurious. But it was peaceful. He felt familiar with this place.","Noah closed the door behind him and exhaled slowly.","\"So... this is my current home,\" he muttered under his breath.","For now, at least.","Just when he thought about resting for a while, his mobile started to ring.","Beep!","Beep!","Noah took out his mobile to check who it was.","\"Father?\"","His eyes widened slightly."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Maybe His Family Is Not That Bad","paragraphs":["Noah remained frozen in place for a few seconds, staring at the screen of his phone as it continued to ring.","His heartbeat quickened slightly. After a brief hesitation, he inhaled quietly and pressed the accept button.","He lifted the phone to his ear. For a moment, there was only faint static from the other side.","Then a heavy and indifferent voice came through.","\"Noah.\"","Just hearing that single word made his back stiffen unconsciously.","\"I got to know about what happened during your exploration... about how you were injured.\"","The voice remained cold. Calm. Distant.","\"Are you okay?\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly. He was shocked. It was his father. Duke Eldritch, the person who exiled him from the family. But now he was calling and asking about his health.","He didn’t know how to react to this situation. He didn’t say anything at first.","The voice spoke again, a little firmer this time.","\"Noah. Are you listening?\"","\"...Yes,\" Noah replied quickly, steadying his voice. \"I’m fine.\"","He responded abruptly. There was silence on the other end. Not the comfortable kind. Just a quiet pause that felt heavy.","Then his father spoke again. \"The academy will start soon.\"","His tone remained the same strict and composed.","\"If you do well... and get into the top ranks... then I might be able to take you back into the family.\"","Noah’s fingers tightened slightly around the phone.","\"But your mother is still against that,\" his father continued. \"I will try to convince her if you become top-ranked in the academy.\"","Another short pause.","\"At least I hope you can achieve that. Even if it’s hard, it’s only good for you.\"","His voice did not soften. It did not waver.","\"Take care. If you need money, just message me.\"","Before Noah could respond, the call ended. The line went silent.","Noah slowly lowered the phone from his ear. The screen had already gone dark.","\"What just happened in seven hells? Did my father just call me... ask about my health... even tell me a way to get back into the family and tell me to ask for money if needed?\" He recounted everything.","But what made him the happiest was the money... he could ask for money whenever he needed from the father of this life.","\"Hahahah!\" Suddenly, Noah started to laugh like an idiot.","\"Oh God, it’s much better. I thought I needed to face some family arc myself... getting into family drama with my bad parents. But it seems they don’t hate me... they just had to exile me for political reasons... wait, it’s my father who doesn’t seem to hate me. But Mother... she’s still angry.\"","Noah lay on his bed. He covered his face with his palm.","\"Hah... for now, I need to focus on the academy. I have no desire to go back to the family or anything. But it might be useful to be part of the Duke family... so I still have to do it.\"","Noah lay there while thinking about his future plan of action.","The academy would start next week. It was currently the first month of the year 2048.","The name of the academy was Novaris Academy.","The most prestigious academy in the Aurelian Imperium Empire. Located in a city named Novaris. Yes, its name was based on the academy.","At least that much was what was written on the internet.","Noah had checked about that.","This year was supposed to be the same year when the main protagonist of this game would enter the academy. So, of course, this year must be special compared to other years.","’I need to get ready and leave for Novaris City this Saturday.’","The academy would start next Monday. Today was Tuesday.","Noah really didn’t want to attend this academy, but he had no choice. The world would be in chaos for sure. If he needed to get stronger, he needed to attend the academy where the main acts of this game would occur.","He needed to make some contribution to get rewards from the so-called useless system, which might be his cheat. Giving him rewards that could help him grow beyond what he could imagine.","’Shit, I am really cooked. I have no knowledge or any guide. How can I survive in this world?’","After thinking for a while, Noah decided to push those thoughts aside and take a nap.","’I will sleep for a while.’","He was mentally exhausted. So sleep came to him instantly.","---","Noah slowly opened his eyes.","For a few seconds, he stared blankly at the ceiling, his mind still hazy from sleep.","Then he turned his head toward the bedside table and grabbed his phone.","3:30 PM.","He blinked twice.","\"I slept that long...\"","His body felt lighter than before. The mental exhaustion had eased a little. The headache from earlier was almost gone.","He sat up on the bed and stretched his arms slightly.","\"No point wasting time.\"","If he was really going to survive in this world. Especially with the academy starting next week. Then resting alone wouldn’t help.","He needed strength. He needed control over his mana. He needed experience.","Noah stood up and adjusted the same navy-blue t-shirt and black trousers he had worn earlier. He didn’t bother changing. These were comfortable enough for light training.","After slipping on his shoes, he grabbed his phone and wallet, then stepped out of the apartment.","The hallway was quiet as usual.","He took the elevator down and walked out of Silvercrest Residences.","The evening air was cool. The sun was still up but slowly beginning its descent.","Noah walked out of the residential colony, hands in his pockets.","Not far from the complex, just about a ten-minute walk away stood a large building made of reinforced glass and dark steel panels.","A glowing sign hung above the entrance.","Crythos Combat & Mana Training Center","In this world, training centers were as common as gyms back on Earth.","Except here, they were more advanced. Also more expensive. Good thing that previous Noah had take one month membership.","Inside, people didn’t just lift weights.","They trained with swords, spears, shields, elemental spells, and mana control techniques.","There were specialized compartments designed to handle mana bursts. Reinforced floors. Impact-resistant walls.","Of course, the cost was quite high. Mana-infused equipment wasn’t cheap. Noah stopped in front of the building and looked up at it.","\"Well... I guess this is where my suffering begins.\"","He exhaled and stepped inside. The interior was spacious and modern.","To the left, there was a regular gym area. Rows of enhanced weight machines, free weights, treadmills, and resistance platforms designed to measure physical stats.","To the right were private training compartments separated by thick transparent barriers glowing faintly with protective runes.","Farther inside were weapon racks, training swords, spears, staves, even practice bows. All made from special alloy materials designed to withstand mana infusion.","Several people were already training. Some were practicing sword forms.","Some were meditating cross-legged, mana faintly swirling around their bodies.","Others were sparring inside enclosed compartments, flashes of elemental light flickering with every clash.","Noah felt a small spark ignite inside him. This felt right. ’This place is amazing.’","He walked toward the reception counter.","Time to start preparing.","Novaris Academy wasn’t going to be kind to an exiled young master."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Training (1)","paragraphs":["After completing his entry at the reception, Noah was directed toward the changing area. The training center also provided clothes specifically designed for training.","Inside the spacious locker room, one corner was neatly arranged with multiple sets of sportswear in different sizes.","They were clean, well-maintained, and neatly folded.","Noah walked over and selected a set that fit him perfectly. It was entirely black—light, flexible, and comfortable against his skin.","After changing, he tied his hair back loosely and stepped out toward the training floor.","He entered an open training area.","Before touching any weapons, he began with basic stretching.","He rolled his shoulders slowly, feeling the joints loosen. He stretched his arms across his chest, then behind his back. He bent forward, stretching his hamstrings, then rotated his waist to warm up his core.","After that, he did light exercises. Push-ups, squats, and a short burst of jumping drills to get his blood flowing.","His breathing gradually steadied. His muscles warmed up.","When the stretching was done, Noah moved toward the weapon racks.","Rows of training weapons were displayed neatly.","’What should I try first?’ he wondered.","He stood there for a moment, thinking.","Then his hand reached out.","Noah picked up a long sword.","The hilt felt cold against his palm. The weight was balanced, not too heavy, not too light.","’Let’s practice both. I’ll do sword basics first and then spear.’","He stepped into an empty practice zone and took a simple stance.","One step forward. His grip firm on hilt. He began with basic slashes.","He did horizontal cut first. Then vertical cut. Diagonal slash.","At first, his movements felt slightly stiff, as if his body remembered but his mind was still catching up. But gradually, something began to click.","The muscle memory of the previous Noah surfaced. He adjusted his footing. His wrist control improved. He repeated the basic forms again and again.","’This feels good!’ Noah thought with smile.","He Slashed, then recover. Step forward. Turn to side. He also focused on his footwork. Not only sword basics.","Minutes passed.","Sweat slowly began to form on his forehead.","His breathing grew heavier, but he didn’t stop.","He practiced thrusts next. It was precise forward lunges, focusing on control rather than speed.","After nearly half an hour, sweat was pouring down his body. His black training shirt clung to his torso.","Finally, he lowered the sword.","\"Not bad...\" he muttered, though he knew he still lacked refinement. He returned the sword to its place.","’But why i don’t have any techniques despite being from a noble family? Was I not talented enough to learn one?’","He wondered as he reached for a spear.","The long shaft felt different—more reach, more control over distance.","He positioned his hands properly and stepped back into the practice area.","He did basic thrust. The tip of the spear thrusting forward horizontally, cutting the air cleanly.","The he withdraw it. Then taking a Step forward he sweep the spear.","He did basic forms again and again.","The spear movements felt smoother than the sword. His body seemed more comfortable maintaining distance rather than engaging closely.","He practiced forward lunges, low sweeps, and controlled spins to adjust his stance.","Sweat dripped from his chin onto the floor.","His arms started to ache slightly.","\"Hah! Hah!\" Only after his breathing became heavy did he finally stop.","Chest rising and falling, Noah wiped the sweat from his forehead with the back of his hand.","’That felt good. I feel more comfortable while using weapons the more I train.’","Noah kept the spear back on racks and then sat at one corner of the room. He could feel some eyes on him. Well it was natural because of his appearance","’Tch! Being good looking attracts too much attention for no reason. Though I don’t hate it if its women who are looking at me’ He thought.","He was sitting in cross leg position to circulate his mana and meditate.","He straightened his back. Then closed his eyes. Took a slow breath in and exhaled.","He focused inward. Soon, he felt it again.","Something warm stirred in his lower abdomen—near his dantian.","A gentle current.","It began to flow through his veins, spreading across his limbs, chest, and shoulders. Smooth. Subtle. Yet undeniably present.","Mana.","The source of everything in this world.","The more he circulated it, the more refreshed he felt.","’It’s not that hard.’","For simple circulation, at least.","He guided the mana carefully through familiar pathways, following the faint memory left behind by the previous Noah.","The flow stabilized. His breathing slowed. His awareness sharpened more.","But he knew this was only the easy part.","’Now it’s time for the harder part.’","Advancement of the Mana Core is not achieved through mere accumulation. A practitioner must first absorb the ambient mana of the world and refine it into a pure form, for the mana that exists in nature is raw and unstable for the human body.","Once refined, this mana is guided into the core, where it accumulates inside and forms condensed layers around it, gradually increasing its density and capacity. As the layers build, the core becomes saturated with energy, pushing it toward its limit.","Yet accumulation alone is insufficient. The layered mana must be compressed and fused together, expelling hidden impurities and stabilizing the core’s structure.","Only when the core withstands this immense pressure and reaches perfect refinement can one break through to the next stage. At that moment, the core’s color shifts, signifying its evolution.","Noah extended his senses outward. At first, there was nothing.","But soon he felt it.","Tiny particles like faint sparks drifting in the air around him.","It was raw mana in air. He began absorbing it slowly.","The moment the foreign mana entered his body, he felt the difference. It was rough.","It was unstable. It needs refinement to get adaptable for human body.","His brows tightened slightly.","He guided the raw mana toward his core and began refining it as he curculate it, making it adaptable to his body.","It wasn’t smooth like circulating his own mana. It felt like forcing sand through narrow pipes.","His breathing became uneven. Sweat began forming along his forehead. The refining process demanded focus.","It needed precision. One mistake could destabilize the flow.","Then he imagined accumulating the purified mana around his core, forming a thin layer over it.","This process is for gradually increasing core density and capacity.","He tried to compressed the acummulated layer. Condensing it. Then ressing it tighter. The pressure increased. A dull ache formed in his lower abdomen.","His jaw clenched unconsciously. More sweat dripped down his neck.","His black training clothes slowly darkened with moisture.","’This... is harder than I thought.’ The core resisted. The mana around it trembled.","At one point, the flow almost slipped out of control, causing a sharp sting inside his chest.","His breathing faltered. But he didn’t stop. He steadied himself.","He Inhale, exhale. His focus was absolute.","Again, he refined. He decided to just refined and accumulate it in his core. Not trying to compress it.","Minute by minute, the condensed layer around his core grew denser.","His body grew hotter. Sweat rolled down his temples and fell onto the mat beneath him.","His hands trembled slightly, resting on his knees. The hour felt endless.","\"Hah!...hah!\" Noah opened his eyes. His breathing ragged.","’I guess this much is enough for today.’"]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Training (2)","paragraphs":["\"Hah... hah...\"","Noah wiped the sweat from his chin and steadied his breathing.","’I guess this much is enough for today.’","His core felt strained but slightly fuller than before. Not enough to break through but enough to notice small progress.","He slowly stood up.","His legs felt slightly numb from sitting cross-legged for so long, but he shook them lightly and walked toward one of the enclosed mana training compartments.","If he was going to survive the academy. He needed combat application.","Not just theory. Not just meditation.","Inside the training center, several compartments were reinforced specifically for elemental spell practice.","Transparent barriers shimmered faintly with protective runes, preventing stray mana from leaking outside.","Noah stepped into an empty compartment. The door sealed behind him with a soft hum.","In front of him stood several training dummies made of mana-resistant alloy. Faint target circles were marked on their torsos.","He exhaled slowly. ’Two spells.’","Ice Shard.","Frost Bind.","He raised his right hand. First he woykd try to perform Ice Shard.","He focused on the mana inside his core.","His affinity was ice. He only posses single affinity. While some people might posses multiple affinities.","Now his spell, it should be cold, sharp and condensed.","He circulated mana from his core toward his palm, shaping it carefully.","At first, the mana felt unstable. He narrowed his eyes. He imagined compressing cold air into a single point.","The temperature around his hand began to drop. Tiny white particles gathered in front of his palm.","The air shimmered faintly. He felt familiar sensation.","Then a crystalline shard began to form. The same one he had used while running away from bear monster","It was Translucent blue color. Its edges were sharp.","The size, it was about the length of a dagger. ’So this is Ice Shard...’","The structure wavered slightly. He steadied the mana flow. It was lower level spell. So there was no magic circle formed while conjuring the spells. Only higher level and complex spells have magic circles.","Noah told himself. Don’t rush. Stabilize the edges. Harden the core.","The shard solidified. Frost mist curled around his fingers. He aimed at the dummy.","\"Go.\"","With a flick of his wrist, the Ice Shard shot forward. It cut through the air cleanly.","Crack!","It struck the dummy’s chest and embedded halfway inside, thin frost spreading outward from the impact point.","Noah blinked.","’Not bad.’ He thought with small curved of his lips.","But the power was limited. The shard had decent speed, but its penetration wasn’t overwhelming.","He tried again. This time, he poured slightly more mana into it. The formation took longer.","Sweat trickled down his temple. The shard formed slightly larger.","’Nice!’","This one was more sharper. He released it.","The shard flew with same speed.","Bang!","The second shard hit harder, cracking part of the dummy’s outer layer. Frost spread more aggressively this time. Noah smiled slightly.","’Control and output both matter.’ He was getting used to this more better than he thought. At this rate he would become just like previous Noah.","Right now could already feel his mana consumption.","Ice Shard wasn’t too expensive, but repeated use would drain him. Though he was enjoying showing spells.","Now it was time for trying another spell.","’Frost Bind’","This one required control more than power. He raised both hands this time.","Instead of compressing mana into a projectile, he let it spread outward along the ground.","Cold energy flowed from his core, down his arms, through his fingertips. He pressed his palm lightly toward the floor.","The air around him cooled sharply. He imagined freezing the surface.","Locking movement. Restricting the target.","Thin layers of frost began to creep forward across the ground. Like white veins spreading over stone.","He directed it toward the dummy.","The frost reached its feet. Then suddenly surged upward.","Crackling ice climbed the dummy’s legs, wrapping around them tightly. Within seconds, the lower half of the dummy was encased in solid ice.","Noah’s breathing became heavy again. Frost Bind consumed more mana than Ice Shard.","’It’s little harder compared to ice Shard. Also takes more mana’ he thought.","And maintaining it required constant output. He held it for a few seconds longer.","The ice thickened. Then he released the spell.","The frost stopped spreading. The ice slowly began to melt under the compartment’s temperature stabilization system.","Noah lowered his hands.","\"Hah...\"","His chest rose and fell heavily. Mana exhaustion tugged at his core.","’I see...’","Ice Shard was better for direct damage. Frost Bind was for restriction and control.","If used together to immobilize first. Then attack. Or attack from distance while controlling movement.","His eyes sharpened slightly. ’Not bad for a start.’","But the casting speed was still slow. His control was not refined.","And his mana pool. Though decent, it was far from overwhelming. He looked at his palm.","Faint frost still lingered on his skin before fading.","\"I need to practice faster casting.\" He clenched his fist tightly.","If he hesitated even a second in real combat. He would die. He already faced that before. He was saved because if his luck. But it might won’t happen again.","Noah stepped out of the training compartment after a few more low-output attempts to avoid draining himself completely.","His entire body felt heavy. Sweat continued to dripped down his body. He was getting exhausted. But still he was satisfied.","Today, he trained weapons. He refined mana. He practiced spells.","\"Ths only thing remained to try its my Ice Creation ability.\"","He already had good idea how Ice Creation does work. Since he got few memories of Noah.","It also needs mana but with ice Creation he could create anything that of ice. It’s proficiency increases slowly.","He remembered forming a dagger in his hand during fight with monster. That dagger was created by this Ice Creation.","Innate ability. It was something that only few people posses after forming Dormant Core.","’I can try Ice Creation at home. Just trying to make some small things and weapons.’ He thought with smile.","He was excited to try creating various things out of thin air, which were made up of ice.","For the first time since waking up in this world He felt like he was truly preparing. And Novaris Academy was only one week away. He was actually getting excited for academy."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Ice Creation","paragraphs":["Friday evening was quiet.","A faint orange glow from the setting sun filtered through the curtains, painting the living room in warm light. The house was silent except for the soft ticking of the wall clock.","Noah sat cross-legged on the floor.","His palm was extended forward, fingers slightly spread. His back was straight, breathing slow but focused. The air in front of him shimmered faintly as mana gathered at his fingertips.","He was practicing his Ice Creation ability. A thin mist of cold air spread outward.","\"Steady...\" he muttered under his breath.","Mana flowed from his core, traveling through his arm and into his palm. The temperature in the room dropped slightly. Frost began forming in the air. Tiny white particles condensing together.","At first, it was unstable.","’You can do it!’","The forming structure cracked and dissolved into snow-like flakes that fell onto the floor.","\"Tch.\"","He exhaled slowly and tried again.","This time, he controlled the output more carefully. Instead of forcing a large amount of mana at once, he released it in layers—gradual and precise.","Ice began to form again. A narrow shape appeared in the air. A blade outline.","He focused harder.","The hilt solidified first, followed by a straight, translucent blade extending outward. The ice glowed faintly blue under the dim light.","Creating small objects was easy. Daggers? Knives? He could form them within seconds, just like he did while fighting. It didn’t even take a second. The previous Noah was used to making them.","To prove it, he flicked his wrist.","In three seconds, a sharp ice dagger materialized in his grip. Smooth, balanced, deadly.","Another flick, and a second knife formed. It was very simple, efficient, and caused minimal strain.","But a full sword? That was different.","The mana consumption increased exponentially. Stability became harder to maintain. Density required compression.","He needed to make it sharp, give it a perfect shape, and sharpen it to the limit. And this was much harder. To his bad luck, Old Noah had never tried forming a sword.","The only things he used this ability for were forming daggers and huge ice rocks, glacier-like structures with no proper shape. They were easy to make as long as he could provide a good amount of mana.","The half-formed blade in front of him trembled.","Crack.","A fracture ran along its surface.","\"No!\"","The sword shattered into fragments before fully stabilizing, dissolving into frost. Noah wiped the sweat from his forehead.","\"It’s the density...\" he murmured. He finally got an idea of how to make a perfect sword.","In truth, he could create a normal sword. But it wouldn’t be like a real sword. It wouldn’t have the sharpness of a real blade that could cut his enemy. It would just be an ice model of a sword, which he didn’t want. He wanted an ice sword that could cut like a real one.","A weapon wasn’t just shape. It required structural reinforcement. Compressed mana layers within the ice to prevent brittleness.","He closed his eyes briefly and adjusted his approach. This time, he formed the inner core first.","Instead of creating the full shape outwardly, he condensed mana into a thin rod of highly compressed ice. It was dense and compact.","Then, slowly, he layered additional ice around it. The ice formed over the core.","The temperature dropped further. A thin layer of frost crept across the wooden floor beneath him. His breathing grew heavier.","\"Hah... hah...\"","Thirty seconds. Then forty. Almost more than a minute passed.","Finally, a complete sword hovered in his hand.","It was longer than the dagger, thicker, with a solid shaft running down the center. The blade shimmered with faint frost patterns.","He grabbed it. His palm wrapped around the cold hilt of the sword.","It was cold and solid. He gave it a light swing. The air hissed as the blade cut through it.","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"It works.\" Noah had been working on this for the last few days. Finally, he was able to form it perfectly.","Even while holding it, he could feel the drain. Once formed, it wouldn’t need constant mana supply. But in the end, it was ice. If Noah didn’t provide it constant mana, it would slowly melt away due to the high temperature of the surroundings.","After a few swings, cracks began forming near the edge. He dispelled it.","\"That still needs work.\"","Now, the spear. He stood up slowly.","Creating a spear required even more control. Length, balance, flexibility in the shaft, and sharpness at the tip.","He had been studying spear and sword structures online on his mobile. It actually helped him a lot.","He extended both hands this time. Mana surged forward.","Ice formed at the center point between his palms and extended outward in two directions. A long shaft began taking shape.","Unlike the sword, the spear needed flexibility in the middle but hardness at the tip.","He concentrated on differential density—less compression in the shaft, extreme compression at the spearhead.","The forming weapon trembled violently. Sweat poured down his face now. His shirt clung to his back.","Even though he was using the ice element, which was cold, it didn’t stop him from sweating.","It was weird even for him. The reason for his sweat was his training at the training center and then the excessive use of mana here. Also, he was not just using mana to generate the weapon. He also needed focus. Using his brain to the fullest.","\"Hold...\"","The spear lengthened to over six feet. The tip sharpened into a deadly triangular point, glowing faintly.","But just as he finished shaping it, the middle section cracked.","The imbalance in mana flow caused instability. The spear shattered into icy dust.","Noah bent forward slightly, catching his breath.","\"That’s why it takes longer...\"","Daggers and knives were simple constructs. Swords required layered reinforcement.","Spears required structural engineering. He straightened again.","\"I won’t stop here.\" He tried once more.","This time, slower. More controlled.","Layer by layer. A minute passed. Then another. Finally, a complete spear formed in his grasp. He stepped back and thrust it forward.","The tip pierced through the air with a sharp whistle. Frost trailed behind the movement.","He spun it once. The shaft held.","There was cracking, but it was not shattering. A grin spread across his face despite the exhaustion.","\"Now that’s better. Hehe! It seems I do have talent for this.\"","He had been training this for a nearly a week now. And finally, he was able to create them.","But his mana reserves were noticeably lower. His core felt warm, slightly strained.","With a thought, he dispersed the spear into glittering frost particles that slowly faded into the air.","The room returned to normal temperature. Noah sat back down on the floor, breathing heavily.","Creating small weapons was easy. Creating durable battlefield weapons? That still required time... and refinement.","He looked at his open palm.","\"If I can reduce the creation time to a few seconds...\"","His eyes sharpened with determination.","\"...then I won’t need to carry weapons at all.\"","Though he understood one thing: creating swords and spears would slowly become easier as he practiced more.","Over the past few days, Noah had regained more of his memory. He felt like he was watching some kind of movie.","But one thing was for sure.","\"This guy was a real scumbag who was enjoying his luxurious life.\"","Noah was angry and envious of the previous Noah at the same time. He clicked his fingers, and very tiny particles of frost slowly fell onto his face. Giving him a cold sensation.","’This is nice.’ He smile widely.","Tomorrow he needs to leave for the academy."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Novaris City","paragraphs":["The next day, Noah woke up early in the morning at 4 a.m. sharp.","After taking a nice hot bath, he got dressed, wearing a black short-sleeve T-shirt. Over it, he put on a dark brown leather jacket. He wore dark blue jeans and, lastly, white shoes.","He looked at himself in the mirror.","His soft snow white hair were short and messy. Which looks good. Whike crystal clear blue eyes.","\"No matter what I wear... I just look too handsome.\"","A stupid smile formed on his face. He wasn’t being narcissistic... okay, he was really being narcissistic. But it was not his fault. The young man standing in front of the mirror was just too good-looking.","He was extremely handsome.","\"Alright, let’s go now.\"","Noah had already stored his bag and other belongings in his storage ring.","He walked toward the apartment door and stepped out, closing it behind him.","He had already informed the landlord that he would be leaving today. So he went to the counter at the ground-floor entrance. He pressed a button at the counter, and soon a lady in her thirties came out.","He handed her the keycard. Saying goodbye to her, he left the building.","\"Now... I should catch the train.\"","He walked again in the direction of the bus stand. Though he had a good amount of money, he decided to travel by train rather than using the teleportation gates. They were really expensive, but that didn’t mean Noah couldn’t afford them. He had enough money for it.","He wanted to see the city better, so he chose the long way.","---","\"Humm...\"","The fast train slowly came to a stop at the platform of Novaris City.","With a soft mechanical sound, the doors of the train slid open smoothly.","Passengers began stepping out one after another. From the general compartments, people who had traveled short distances exited first. Office workers heading to their jobs, young teenagers on their way to school, and a few couples who seemed to have come to the city for a date.","Those who had traveled long distances came from the reserved coaches, carrying luggage and looking slightly tired from the journey.","From one of those coaches, Noah Eldritch stepped out onto the platform.","The moment both his feet touched the ground, the train doors behind him closed automatically with a sharp hiss. A second later, the platform screen doors slid shut as well, sealing the edge securely.","A warning tone rang out. Then the train began to move again, slowly at first before accelerating down the tracks and disappearing into the distance.","Noah glanced around.","The platform of Novaris City Station was spotless and modern. The floor gleamed under bright white lights. Large digital panels displayed schedules in clean blue text. Transparent glass barriers and sleek steel pillars gave the entire place a futuristic yet elegant design.","He felt a flicker of excitement. It was Saturday afternoon. It had taken hours to reach here.","He had taken the early morning train from Crythos, and after hours of travel, he had finally arrived.","\"This place... is amazing,\" he muttered softly.","After exiting through the ticket gates, he stepped outside the station and into the city.","The view made him pause.","Novaris City was truly beautiful. Tall glass buildings reflected the afternoon sunlight. Wide roads were lined with trees, and clean sidewalks stretched neatly in every direction. The air felt lively yet organized. Busy, but not chaotic.","\"Now that’s some amazing architecture... man, if I can see such things, how can I hate this world?\"","Then he sighed. Suddenly, memories of his family came to him. Not from this world, but from his past world.","He shook his head, trying to put those thoughts aside. Noah pulled out his mobile and checked the map.","The academy was not within walking distance, but a bus route led to a stop close to it.","He followed the directions toward the nearby bus station. Within a few minutes, he reached the designated stop and waited.","The city traffic moved smoothly around him. Soon, a bus arrived with a soft hydraulic sigh.","Noah stepped inside and paid the fare using the machine beside the driver. After confirming the payment, he walked down the aisle and took a window seat.","The bus moved again.","Through the window, he watched the city pass by commercial districts shifting into quieter areas with larger buildings and open spaces.","\"I still have tomorrow as a free day. I can explore this city tomorrow. Then the academy will start on Monday. Well, good thing that students are allowed to go outside the academy campus area.\"","Noah was happy about that. This whole city basically belonged to the academy.","It was Novaris Academy that had been built on land where there was nothing many years ago. Soon, many companies and industries sponsored the academy, opening their businesses here. Most of them belonged to the academy. With time, this place turned into a huge city named after Novaris Academy – Novaris City.","It took around ten minutes to reach his destination.","The bus slowed and stopped. Noah stepped down onto the pavement and once again checked the map on his phone.","\"Just a little further.\"","He followed the indicated route, walking down a broad road lined with tall trees.","And then he saw it. His eyes widened in shock.","The academy stood proudly at the end of a wide stone pathway.","A massive iron gate marked the entrance, intricately designed with elegant patterns woven into its structure.","Beyond it stretched a vast campus. Expansive lawns, towering academic buildings built from white stone, and tall spires that reached toward the sky.","The main building stood at the center like a palace.","Large arched windows reflected the sunlight. Banners bearing the academy’s emblem fluttered gently in the wind. The architecture was a perfect blend of classical grandeur and modern refinement.","It radiated prestige, showing off its power and telling its own history.","Noah stood there quietly for a moment, staring at it.","\"So... this is the Novaris Academy.\"","A faint smile formed on his lips. A new Chapter was about to begin."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Novaris Academy","paragraphs":["Noah entered the academy gate after displaying his admission documents on his mobile. A soft beam of pale blue light swept over his body from head to toe, scanning him in seconds.","A quiet chime followed.","\"Identity verified.\"","He didn’t think much of it and stepped inside.","The campus was massive, stretching far beyond what he had imagined. Beneath his feet lay a wide cobblestone path, each stone evenly cut and polished, looking almost new. The path was spotless, as if it were cleaned every hour.","On both sides spread lush green lawns, trimmed perfectly. Decorative trees lined the walkway at regular intervals, their branches swaying gently in the breeze. Beds of colorful flowers added brightness to the scenery.","It felt more like a royal garden than an academy.","As he walked further, a grand fountain came into view.","It stood at the center of a circular plaza. The structure was carved from white stone, layered in three tiers. From the very top, a column of water shot upward before cascading down into the second tier, then flowing in smooth streams into the wide basin below.","Sunlight reflected off the falling water, creating faint rainbow patterns in the mist. The sound of flowing water echoed softly across the courtyard, calm and rhythmic.","Two curved paths split around the fountain. One leading to the right wing of the campus, the other to the left. A broad staircase directly behind the fountain led straight toward the academy’s main building.","Noah climbed the steps.","The large doors opened automatically as he approached.","Inside, he found himself in a grand hallway with high ceilings and polished marble floors. Tall pillars lined both sides, and banners bearing the academy’s emblem hung between them. The space felt dignified and authoritative.","A few staff members walked past him, carrying files and tablets.","With a thoughtful expression, he muttered, \"I need to go to the office first for registration.\"","’Where might it be?’","After going in the same direction, he looked around and spotted a large digital directory mounted on the wall. It displayed a map of the building along with labeled sections.","\"Administrative Office – Ground Floor, East Wing.\"","With a small nod, he said, \"That makes it easy.\"","He followed the signs pointing toward the East Wing. After walking down a quieter corridor, he found a glass door labeled Administration Office.","He stepped inside.","Behind a long reception desk sat a middle-aged woman wearing formal attire. She looked up as he approached.","With a neutral expression, she asked, \"Yes?\"","Politely, Noah replied, \"I’m a new student. Here for entry registration,\" showing his admission confirmation on his mobile.","She nodded and gestured for him to place his phone on a small scanning pad. The system processed his details quickly.","Calmly, she said, \"Please stand still.\"","A small device beside the desk emitted another scanning light. Within seconds, his information was confirmed.","With a professional tone, she said, \"Registration completed. Place your thumb here.\"","He pressed his thumb onto a small biometric panel.","Moments later, a sleek card slid out from a slot in the desk.","It was a metallic ID card with the academy emblem engraved at the top. His name—Noah Eldritch—was displayed clearly, along with a unique identification code.","She handed it to him and explained, \"This is your student ID. It grants you access to academic buildings, training areas, the library, and your assigned dormitory room. Also, with this, you can use transport in this city freely.\"","She tapped on her screen again.","\"Dormitory Block C. Room 312. The card will unlock your room door.\"","With a grateful expression, Noah said, \"Thank you.\"","With that, he turned and left the office.","As he stepped back into the grand hallway, the weight of the card in his hand felt symbolic.","He was officially a student of Novaris Academy.","Now, the real beginning awaited him.","---","The path that led to the dormitory area was on the left side of the fountain. Soon, he found the dormitory buildings. They were spread wide.","Looking around in awe, he muttered, \"Man... this place is too huge.\"","Noah moved to find Block C. Soon, he found it and scanned his card at the counter on the ground floor of the building. He took the elevator and pressed the button for the third floor.","The doors slid open, revealing the corridor of the third floor. He stopped in front of the door marked 312.","With excitement in his eyes, he said, \"This is my new room.\"","Noah scanned the card at the door like a keycard.","The lock opened with a soft beep.","He entered the room. It was dark. Then the lights turned on automatically.","Surprised, he exclaimed, \"Oh! This is better than I thought.\"","It was big. A living room with a balcony. A connected kitchen. A bedroom. It was perfect for living.","With delight, he thought, ’Nice! It also has a TV.’","Noah checked his bedroom. There was a single bed, a desk near the window, and a bathroom.","With satisfaction, he said, \"This is perfect. Now let’s arrange my things and get something to eat.\"","It was late afternoon, so he was hungry and wanted to eat something.","He opened the cupboard in the bedroom, took out his bag from the storage ring, and started arranging his clothes inside.","Once he was done, he left the dormitory room.","He wondered where he could get something to eat. Did he need to go outside the academy?","But he was happy to see that there were many shops inside the academy campus. Students might hardly want to leave the academy. Of course, they were limited, but good enough.","After roaming around the campus, he got to know a few things. Most places were cafés, cake shops, ice cream stalls, and similar stores.","There were no huge restaurants.","He decided to ask an ice cream vendor inside the campus.","The vendor looked at him casually as Noah asked, \"Excuse me, where can I get proper food?\"","The vendor replied kindly, \"There’s a cafeteria inside the campus. You can eat there for free with your student ID.\"","Feeling pleased, Noah thought, ’Well, that’s good.’","He then headed toward the cafeteria."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: First Day At Novaris Academy (1)","paragraphs":["In the blink of an eye, Monday came.","Noah was lying on the bed. His white hair was messy, eyes closed. His long eyelashes enhanced his appearance. His face had a perfect shape.","Slowly, his eyelids twitched as they started to open.","Everything was blurry. He blinked a few times to get accustomed to his sight.","Yawn~","He yawned, stretching his arms up.","’It’s already morning... and Monday. The first day of the academy.’ He thought for a while, lying there.","He was really excited for this, but now that it was the first day of the academy, he suddenly started to feel nervous.","Can he do well? Can he be on good terms with the main characters? Can he survive in the academy? Those dangerous scenarios? Which he has no idea about? Will his actions cause some butterfly effect?","’Fuck! No point in thinking about that. The biggest problem will be my own personality.’","He got up from the bed with a sour face.","If he had to tell what kind of person Noah... no, not the previous Noah, but Aron who is now Noah. If he had to describe himself, then all he could say was troublemaker.","That was his reputation in his past life.","Of course, it was not as if he was trying to do some bad things. Rather, he was just doing normal things, but they always led to problems. Maybe it was just his luck that was bad.","Pushing those thoughts aside, Noah entered the bathroom. He brushed his teeth, then took a nice bath.","Then he opened the cupboard in the bedroom. Yesterday, the academy had sent him his academy uniform. They were a total of two in number.","He took one out and started to wear it.","Soon, he was standing in front of the mirror and checking his handsome features.","The uniform he was wearing consisted of a white inner shirt and a red tie. It had a tailored gray blazer coat that he wore over the shirt. Red piping ran along the edges of the collar and cuffs of the blazer. Three subtle rune patterns were woven into the inside lining; they worked for slight protection of the body.","Noah just ran his hands through his hair, arranging it enough to look good.","Even if he kept it messy, he would still look handsome. No point in trying to makeover.","\"Okay, it’s time for the academy.\"","Noah left his dormitory.","---","Noah walked out of the dormitory buildings, the morning air cool and fresh against his face. The campus felt different today. It was livelier.","Groups of students in identical uniforms moved along the pathways, some chatting excitedly, others looking just as nervous as he felt.","The cobblestone path stretched ahead of him, leading toward the academic section of the academy. Sunlight filtered through the tall trees, casting shifting shadows across the ground.","Noah slipped his hands into his pockets and walked at a relaxed pace.","’Calm down,’ he told himself.","As he passed through a small commercial area inside the campus, a few shops were already open.","The smell of freshly brewed coffee drifted through the air. A bakery displayed warm bread behind glass panels. A convenience stall nearby had snacks stacked neatly on shelves.","Noah slowed down.","\"...Might as well.\"","He stepped toward the shop and casually picked up a few packets of chips, some candies, and a pack of roasted peanuts.","The shopkeeper glanced at him briefly while scanning the items.","After paying, Noah stepped aside and discreetly stored the snacks inside his storage ring.","’For emergency situations,’ he thought seriously.","Then he resumed walking.","He took out his student ID card and examined it. On the back, a small digital display lit up when he tapped it. His schedule appeared along with his classroom number.","\"First-year Class A-1 – Room 1-07.\"","\"Hmm.\"","He looked around, searching for directional signs. Large boards were placed at intersections across the campus, indicating different academic blocks.","After walking for several minutes and asking one passing student for confirmation, he finally located the correct building.","It was larger than the others nearby, built from the same white stone as the main structure but with a more academic feel than administrative.","Students were entering through its tall doors.","Noah climbed the short staircase and stepped inside.","The interior hallway was wide and filled with rows of lockers along the walls. Conversations echoed softly around him. Some students laughed nervously, some stood quietly reviewing notes, and others simply looked around curiously.","He followed the room numbers displayed above each doorway.","1-03.","1-05.","Then.","1-07.","Noah stopped walking.","In front of him stood a huge double door made of dark polished wood, engraved with subtle rune markings near the frame.","This was it. His classroom.","For a brief moment, he just stood there, staring at the door.","’Alright... let’s see what kind of chaos awaits.’","Taking a slow breath, Noah reached for the handle. He slide opened the door.","\"Hah... okay.\" Noah entered the classroom. Closed the door behind.","He saw descending rows, piling upon rows of exquisitely arranged desks. He could almost taste the vibrancy of the students occupying these desks.","The whole interior was neat and spotless, almost as if it was shining.","Kids were chatting among themselves, friends were catching up with each other, and some diligent students readied themselves for the first day with their heads buried in their books.","But then their eyes fell on the newcomer.","Noah, who had just entered, felt weird. He stopped at the door, gazing at everyone while they stared at him.","The classroom went silent when they saw him.","Noah blinked and smiled nervously, not knowing why they were looking at him like that. Actually, he already had an idea, but he never thought it would have this much effect.","Noah didn’t remain there and went to the back side of the class, chose the last row, and sat down on it.","Many started to murmur about Noah with displeased expressions, while a few gave curious looks like they didn’t know why everyone was talking like this.","While Noah just dismissed the stares, closed his eyes, and waited for the class to start soon."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: First Day At Novaris Academy (2)","paragraphs":["Noah sat comfortably in the last row. From this place, he could see the whole class without any problem.","’Interesting.’","Soon his eyes landed on the person sitting in the front of the right-side row.","A man with blonde-colored hair. He was taller than six feet. His body leaned toward the bulky side. The uniform fit him perfectly, showcasing his well-built physique. His skin was tanned, and his eyes were hazel in color.","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly.","’That guy...’","Memories surfaced in his mind.","Before transmigrating into this game world, Noah. No, Aron had only seen the character list and basic descriptions.","That blonde-haired guy was Leonard Valtier, one of the main supporting characters of the story.","Leonard was known for using a greatsword—an enormous blade that required both strength and stamina to wield. In the game, he was portrayed as the \"shield of the protagonist,\" a frontline powerhouse who overwhelmed enemies with raw strength and unshakable defense.","He belonged to a noble family famous for producing knights for generations.","’A tank-type fighter... loyal, straightforward, strong,’ Noah recalled silently.","Leonard was the type who valued honor and strength above everything else.","Noah shifted his gaze away calmly. If Leonard was here...","Then the important characters should also be nearby.","His eyes wandered across the classroom once more until they paused at another corner.","There.","A girl sitting by the window.","Long, flowing violet-colored hair cascaded down her back like silk. Under the sunlight streaming through the glass, it shimmered faintly. Her golden eyes were calm yet sharp, observing the room quietly. Her facial features were delicate, almost unreal.","She was beautiful. No, she was breathtaking. Her figure leaned toward voluptuous, but Noah decided not to focus on it. Yeah. He was not some lustful man!","Even compared to noble daughters known for their elegance and refinement, her beauty stood on equal footing, if not above them.","’So she’s here too...’","Her name was Arisha Willow.","One of the female leads of the game.","Unlike many prominent students in this academy, Arisha did not come from a noble background. She was born into a normal family. Commoners with no political power or prestigious lineage.","And yet, through sheer talent and hard work, she had earned her place here. Unlike how Noah entered with his family name, she entered by her talent, by passing the entrance exam.","In the game’s character description, she was known for her exceptional affinity with magic, especially elemental control. Her growth curve was monstrous.","A commoner with overwhelming talent.","Noah leaned back slightly in his chair.","’Main supporting character... female lead...’","It seemed he had truly stepped into the core of the story.","And this was only the first day.","Just then, someone else entered the classroom.","Two girls entered the classroom.","\"This is our classroom. It’s big!\" one of them said cheerfully.","A wide smile was on her face since she entered the room. Her long dark brown hair was tied in a single braid, which rested on her right shoulder. Her blue eyes were sparkling with excitement.","\"Hey Emma! Wait for me.\" Behind her followed another girl. She was tall, around 176 centimeters. Her long hair was loose. It was long and golden-blonde in color. Her eyes were soft pink in color. They were enchanting. Her face was extremely beautiful. Below her face, the two heavy things she was carrying were a perfect pair. Held by her academy uniform, they had a perfect round shape.","\"Oh come on, Lyria! I was just too excited for my first day at the academy. Haha!\" Emma said with the same cheerful expression.","Her name was Lyria Sunweave.","Noah considered Emma as the playful and mischievous character of the game.","’This is serious. Can’t tell who has a bigger pair... Arisha or Lyria.’","Noah’s eyes once again widened at seeing another beautiful lady.","Both of those women were female leads of this game.","It was true that Lyria was the one who attracted Noah more than Emma.","The two girls soon moved toward the front row and sat on it,","choosing to be front benchers.","Just when Noah was enjoying the view, he felt a cold stare from somewhere.","Noah frowned at the strange gaze.","A chill ran down his spine.","The atmosphere around him suddenly felt heavier, as if the temperature had dropped by several degrees.","He slowly turned toward the direction from where he felt someone was trying to bore a hole through him with their eyes.","And then he saw her.","Dark midnight-blue hair waved freely up to her waist. Her eyes were the same as a forest, emerald in color.","Her name was Ophelia Thornveil.","Noah stiffened the moment their eyes met.","His heartbeat skipped.","Fragments of old memories surged violently through his mind. Images not his own, yet belonging to this body. The humiliation. The scandal. The accusation.","She was none other than his ex-fiancée. The daughter of Duke Thornveil.","The same woman whom the previous Noah had tried to assault and because of whom he was exiled from the family.","’Shit!’","Noah cursed inwardly while looking at her.","For a brief second, he felt as if those emerald eyes could slice him apart.","There was no warmth in them.","Only coldness.","Only hatred.","It was suffocating.","He was really shocked at his luck—for her to be in the same class as him.","When Aron saw the first character from the game, Leonard, he understood that he might be in the same class as the main characters.","But he was not too surprised. It was a normal thing in most novels.","’Fuck! How can I forget about her? She’s also a supporting character.’","One of the biggest reasons why Noah had downloaded the game named Odyssey of Eternal Gods’ War was because it had romance and a harem.","Though he remembered seeing Ophelia on the character list, she was not a female lead, but rather a supporting character.","But there was always a route for side characters.","Noah had to accept the fact that the old Noah was one hell of a lucky bastard.","Parents who let you enjoy their money. One did not have to worry about the future, since Noah also had an older brother who was the next heir of his family.","Noah did not have to worry and could enjoy his luxurious life.","And yet, he also had a beautiful lady like Ophelia as his fiancée.","’I am now jealous of this bastard! Why did he even try to assault her, this horny bastard?’","If that guy had been a decent man, then the current Noah might have been very lucky. But now he had to face the consequences of all the deeds done by the previous Noah.","Ophelia stared at Noah with cold eyes filled with hatred for a while, then turned forward.","’Hah... I’m cooked... Oh, there was also another supporting character who was like the main protagonist’s rival or at least he considered the protagonist as a rival. If I remember correctly, his name was Kaelan Nightfall.’","It didn’t take much time for him to push those bad thoughts aside.","’Well, whatever. I really don’t want to think about them anymore. I should relax a little before class gets started.’","Noah pulled out the peanuts from his storage ring. They were roasted ones, packed in a packet. Noah tore it open and kept it under the desk, where there was a shelf-like structure. He took a few of them and put them inside his mouth.","Munch!","Munch!","They had a mildly sweet taste with a deep roasted flavor."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: First Day At Novaris Academy (3)","paragraphs":["The classroom was filled with the sound of chatter.","Noah sat calmly while eating some light snacks.","As he ate the peanuts, they made a light crunchy sound. It was not too loud. It was barely audible.","Noah took out his mobile and started scrolling through the academy guidelines. It was huge. He thought it might come in useful. If he knew the rules of this academy, he could control himself from causing trouble.","His other hand picked up a peanut and tossed it into his mouth.","Bad habits die hard. Noah had a bad habit of eating during lectures at his university, sitting in the back rows and munching on something he brought in his bag.","\"This is so huge... I am really bored reading all this.\"","Just then, a sharp voice echoed loudly through the classroom.","\"Attention!\"","Instinctively, Noah put his mobile into his storage ring.","His eyes gazed forward.","Standing behind the podium was a breathtaking beauty.","She had long light blue color hair. It fell loose down her back like a waterfall, reaching her waist.","Her eyes were a beautiful violet color, like crystal. Her skin was fair. She stood tall, around six feet two inches. Her face was mature and extremely beautiful. A mole rested under the corner of her left eye. Her figure... Noah had no words to describe it.","She wore a tailored charcoal blazer, perfectly fitted to her dangerously voluptuous frame, the fabric woven with faint silver threads that shimmered only when mana brushed against them.","Beneath it was a high-collared ivory blouse, buttoned neatly to the top, the collar clasped with a small sapphire brooch engraved with a subtle rune of amplification.","Her skirt fell just below the knee—sleek and black. Her stockings were dark and seamless, disappearing into polished leather ankle boots with a modest heel.","Noah did not even notice when she had entered.","Everyone was surprised by her sudden appearance, and within seconds, the classroom went completely silent.","Noah stopped chewing for a moment, mesmerized by her beauty.","It was as if she had appeared out of thin air.","Most of the students looked shocked, clearly not having sensed her presence at all.","However, a few students were not surprised. They remained calm, as if they had sensed her arrival beforehand.","Some students tried to murmur quietly, but the instructor suddenly raised her hand and struck her palm against the surface of the podium.","Bang!","A visible ripple of mana burst outward from the impact.","The shockwave traveled across the classroom in a split second.","The air trembled. Desks vibrated slightly.","Every student froze at this sudden change in atmosphere.","Noah’s eyes widened in shock as he felt the wave brush past him. It was not harmful, but the pressure behind it was overwhelming. He instinctively leaned slightly backward in his seat.","However, a few students remained unaffected, sitting normally as if nothing had happened.","Noah noticed that.","’So these are the monstrous beings...’","The woman’s cold violet eyes swept across the classroom.","\"My name is Morgana Celestine,\" she said calmly, her tone strict and cruel.","\"I will be your head instructor.\"","She paused for a second. \"I am an S-rank hero. Currently at the Astral Core Level—Low.\"","A faint murmur almost rose again, but her gaze alone silenced it.","She held a high position in the kingdom’s army. Even among S-rank heroes, she was considered powerful.","Morgana’s eyes scanned the class again.","\"The fact that almost all of you failed to sense my presence,\" she said coldly, \"is pathetic.\"","Her gaze lingered briefly on a few students. The same ones who had not reacted to her entrance.","\"Except for a handful.\"","Her tone remained emotionless, yet sharp like a blade.","\"From today onward, you will understand what true discipline is.\"","After finishing her brief introduction, she took out a sleek tab device.","\"I will now take attendance,\" she said. \"When I call your name, you will come forward and scan your ID on this tab. Your rank information will be added to your card.\"","The classroom remained completely silent.","She began calling names, announcing each student’s academy rank before their name.","\"Mark Burgermus! Academy Rank 1987!\"","\"Present, Ma’am.\"","He walked toward her, scanned his ID, and returned to his seat.","\"Amisha Loudricks! Academy Rank 1857! Come forward!\"","\"Present!\"","At the sound of her name, Amisha rose from her seat and made her way toward the podium. A faint tension lingered in her expression. Perhaps she was worried about her unusually low rank.","But what she didn’t know was that the rankings at the beginning of the year held little real meaning.","After the monthly exams, this ranking might change, Noah thought while looking forward.","Morgana resumed the attendance.","\"Noah Eldritch! Academy Rank 1786!\"","\"Coming!\" he replied.","Noah quietly swallowed the remaining peanuts in his mouth.","He stood up calmly and walked toward the podium.","As he approached Morgana, he could feel her presence more clearly. It was suffocating.","He took out his ID card and placed it on the tab.","A faint light scanned it.","He retrieved it.","There was a slight change in Morgana’s expression when she saw his name.","It was subtle, but noticeable. Of course, it was because of his bad reputation.","Noah maintained a calm face. Honestly, he didn’t care about his reputation.","\"Thank you,\" he said politely.","Then he turned and walked back to his seat. The ranking continued.","\"Ken Takeane! Academy Rank 1122!\"","\"Present!\"","\"Steven Hawking! Academy Rank 1289!\"","\"Here!\"","While Noah click on his ID as information appeared on it.","---","Name:Noah Eldritch","Academy Ranking: 1786/2000","Rank: Dormant (High)","Potential: Refined Core (High)","Class: A-1","---","\"Isacc Newtella! Academy Rank 756!\"","\"Present!\"","One after another, students stood as their names and ranks were called. Morgana continued the roll call steadily, her voice firm and unhurried.","\"Marina Lockhart! Academy Rank 124!\"","\"Yes!\"","Finally, Noah noticed someone from another race. Marina was an elf with long blonde hair. She was not alone. There were a few others, like beastmen. But their number was very low. In this class, there might be hundreds of students, but only around ten of them were from other races.","The academy was global. They had allowed students from other races to enroll a few years ago, except Demons.","As always, Demons were the villains in this world.","\"Elijah Noctis! Academy Rank 115!\"","\"Yes!\"","She continued calling names.","\"Ophelia Thronveil! Academy Rank 29!\"","\"Present, Ma’am!\"","Murmurs spread once more among the students when a top thirty rank was announced.","Morgana, however, remained unimpressed. Unlike the students, she did not place much faith in these early rankings.","From experience, she knew how unreliable they were at this stage.","\"Lyria Sunweave! Academy Rank 13!\"","\"Okay!\"","Slowly, the rankings moved toward the top students.","\"Leonard Valtier! Academy Rank 11!\"","As expected, the main characters were placed at the top ranks.","Then Morgana called,","\"Arisha Willow! Academy Rank 9!\"","Arisha, the violet-haired beauty, walked forward to scan her ID.","Then came,","\"Kael Knightfall! Academy Rank 2!\"","Here it came. The rival of the protagonist. A man with short black hair and dark blue eyes.","’Well, the other top rankers will be in other classes. But we got Rank 9, 2, and 1. Three top ten rankers. Nice!’","Noah had already considered that the protagonist would be in his class.","Then finally came Rank One. \"Damien Ashworth! Academy Rank 1!\"","There was no reply. No one stood up. She called again.","\"Damien Ashworth!\"","Still silence.","Her eyes turned colder.","She called his name a third time, louder. Just as she was about to call again.","The classroom door suddenly opened.","Bang!","A young, handsome man stood at the entrance.","He had black hair and hazel eyes. He was tall, with a good build. His chest was rising and falling rapidly, as if he had run all the way there.","\"I’m... sorry for being late,\" he said, slightly out of breath.","And just like that, the true protagonist had arrived."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: First Day At Novaris Academy (4)","paragraphs":["\"May I come in?\" the protagonist, whose name was Damien, asked with a small smile on his face.","Morgana folded her arms beneath her chest, her posture straight and imposing. Her violet eyes were cold and strict as they stared at him.","\"No,\" she replied flatly, her expression unmoved. \"You are not allowed to enter. You are late.\"","A faint murmur spread across the classroom.","Damien blinked once, still standing at the doorway.","With a calm expression, he said, \"Master, it was only ten minutes.\"","Morgana’s eyes sharpened slightly. \"Ten minutes,\" she repeated, her voice turning colder. \"In a battlefield, ten minutes is enough for an entire squad to be wiped out.\"","The air inside the classroom grew tense.","Some students exchanged confused glances.","Master?","Did he just call her master?","Damien sighed softly, looking slightly awkward. \"I-I was fighting a E+ rank monster. Then there was traffic near the inner gate. And the guard insisted on rechecking my ID.\"","\"Excuses,\" Morgana cut him off sharply. \"An elite should account for delays before they happen.\"","Damien’s smile twitched slightly. \"You’re being too strict on the first day.\"","\"I am always strict,\" she replied without hesitation, her gaze unwavering. \"That is why you are alive.\"","The classroom went completely silent.","The students stared at the two of them in disbelief.","Was the top-ranked student... actually her disciple?","Damien scratched the back of his head with a helpless expression. \"Master, you trained me yourself. You know I wouldn’t be late without reason.\"","Meanwhile, Noah was enjoying the scene. It felt like he was watching a TV series of some webnovel.","’This looks more fun.’ He thought while watching everything with interest.","He continued to throw peanuts into his mouth, chewing them and enjoying the show.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"And yet, you are late.\"","With a dramatic expression, Damien placed a hand over his chest. \"Are you really going to make your favorite disciple stand outside like a criminal?\"","A few students gasped quietly. Favorite disciple?","Morgana’s expression darkened.","\"Do not twist words, Damien Ashworth,\" she said coldly. \"You are my disciple, yes. That is precisely why I will not tolerate your indiscipline.\"","The pressure in the room subtly increased.","Damien gave a helpless smile. \"Then please allow this unworthy disciple to enter and accept punishment afterward.\"","A pause.","The two locked eyes.","Munch.","Munch.","The tension between them was strange. Not hostile, but charged with familiarity.","Finally, Morgana exhaled softly.","\"You will run fifty laps around the training grounds after class,\" she said sternly. \"And you will report to me personally in the evening.\"","Damien’s shoulders slumped slightly in disbelief. \"Fifty? Master, that’s cruel.\"","Munch","Crunch","\"Seven—\"","Suddenly, Morgana stopped scolding Damien. Her sharp violet eyes turned toward Noah, meeting his crystal blue eyes.","Noah stopped biting whatever he was eating. His breath paused for a moment. A shiver ran down his spine.","’What? Why is she looking at me like that?’","Noah instinctively pushed the wrapper of peanuts under the desk toward the student who was sitting beside him.","The guy beside him gave him a confused look.","\"Noah Eldritch!\" Her voice echoed through the classroom.","Noah stood up immediately.","\"Yes, ma’am!\" He straightened his back.","Morgana looked at him coldly. \"This is your first day at the academy. The first lecture of it... and you are blatantly eating something with that smiling face, like you are enjoying some show.\"","’Shit! She knew it!’","Students soon started to murmur.","Things like he sure is troublesome.","First day and already causing unnecessary issues.","And more.","Even the protagonist looked at Noah with interest.","The attention that Damien was getting soon turned to Noah.","For what?","Because he was just comfortably sitting while eating some peanuts and enjoying the show.","He gulped down whatever he had not chewed.","With a respectful expression, he said, \"I’m sorry for my behavior, Instructor Morgana.\"","Noah bowed for forgiveness.","Again, this made several people shocked because the way Noah spoke seemed surprising to them. He was talking very politely.","Morgana studied him for a while, her expression unreadable. Then she sighed softly.","\"Since this is the first day, I will overlook it. But if I find you doing something like this again, you will be punished.\"","Noah nodded immediately. \"As you say, Instructor. I will behave from now on.\"","\"You may sit down.\"","Noah sat down calmly.","\"And you... you may enter,\" Morgana said, turning her cold gaze back to Damien, who was still standing at the door.","Damien bowed his head slightly with a faint smile. \"Thank you, Master.\"","He walked inside, the door closing behind him.","Every pair of eyes followed him.","Whispers immediately erupted in low tones.","\"So he’s really her disciple...\"","\"That’s why he’s Rank 1...\"","\"No wonder...\"","Again, everyone’s attention turned to Damien, but not as strongly as before, because some of the students were murmuring about Noah.","Though many main characters were looking at Damien with interest.","Meanwhile, Noah quietly took his packet of peanuts and put it inside his storage ring.","’I will eat this later.’","Noah, sitting at the back, leaned against his chair with a faint grin.","’But this is really amazing.’","The legendary hero of this game. The only being having the potential to reach Mythical Core and the top-ranked student had just been arguing as master and disciple on the first day.","This was far more entertaining than reading academy guidelines.","Noah had just been scolded by Morgana, but that did not matter to him. It was not his first time getting scolded. During his college days, he had heard things like this many times.","Right now, he was more interested in these characters of the game who were now alive.","’The protagonist truly lives a different life,’ Noah thought.","Meanwhile, after scanning his ID, Damien calmly walked toward the front row, as if nothing unusual had happened.","Morgana returned behind the podium, her expression once again emotionless.","\"Attendance for today has been done,\" she said coldly.","And just like that, the classroom was reminded. This was no ordinary academy. And this was no ordinary instructor."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Weapon Selection","paragraphs":["\"Now that the attendance is done, we should move toward the next important thing,\" Morgana said in a calm but authoritative tone.","\"You all get a chance to choose a weapon for yourselves. I know many of you might already possess one, but some of you might not, mostly those who came from normal backgrounds. So all of you can choose one weapon. Even those who already possess one. Think of it as a formality from the academy.\"","After saying that, Morgana walked toward the door. She glanced over her shoulder at the class.","\"Now follow me, all of you.\"","Everybody in the class got up from their seats and started to follow Morgana.","Noah also got up from his seat. He remained last, then quietly followed them.","After a while, arriving in front of a large room, Morgana stopped. She stood in front of everyone.","Then she took something out of her own storage ring. It was her Instructor ID. She scanned her own ID at the panel beside the huge door.","The door slid open immediately.","A large room appeared before everyone, and the diversity of weapons present there left Noah and everyone else speechless.","– \"Wow! Look how huge this room is!\"","– \"There are so many weapons!\"","– \"I’ve never seen something like this before!\"","– \"Damn, even weapon shops don’t have this many weapons!\"","Students started to chatter after seeing the room.","Noah wanted to say something as well, but for now he was a loner.","\"Tch!\" He clicked his tongue.","’I need to make some friends. Excluding main characters.’","Then he focused on the room.","The room was filled with many different kinds of weapons. There were shelves along the walls and tables in the middle, all made of strong metal. On them were arranged various weapons.","From nunchucks to broadswords, spears to bows. Every sort of weapon was neatly laid out according to its size and displayed before the students.","\"There’s a wide selection of weapons here, so feel free to choose what you deem to be the best fit for you. Choose wisely,\" Morgana said in a strict, cold tone.","Noah was really impressed by the scene.","There were so many weapons that he couldn’t even tell what some of them were. There were many varieties.","Then Morgana’s expression turned slightly serious as she added another warning. \"Also, everyone be careful. I’d be very careful if I were you. If you damage any weapon present here, you better be ready to pay up to 500,000 Zeni.\"","Seeing the excited expressions of the students in the class, Morgana immediately poured cold water on their excitement as she pointed out the price of each weapon.","’Crazy! Up to 500,000 Zeni!’ Noah was scared after hearing that price. Well, he was not the only one who felt like that.","Some students couldn’t help but flinch as they started looking at the weapons like they were some sort of divine artifacts.","\"I advise using a weapon that is suitable for you so that you don’t risk damaging it,\" Morgana continued calmly.","\"Also, don’t worry. Once you choose a weapon, it will be yours. So even if you damage it or break it, you won’t have to pay. But you won’t be getting a new one until the second semester. So experimenting is good, but only if you can afford it.\"","Looking at the 150 or so students before her, Morgana smiled faintly and continued further.","\"Before taking a weapon, scan your ID near the small scanners beside each weapon so that you can register your name in the database. After that, take your weapon.\"","Near each weapon, there was a small scanner.","Having finished what she wanted to say, Morgana turned around and stood a little distance away from the students, letting them observe and choose the right weapon for themselves.","Noah was actually excited to see such things.","His eyes darted here and there.","’I already got a sword. So it’s better to have a spear since I don’t have one.’","Noah walked through the huge room, though hall might have been a better word for it.","He wanted to choose a weapon that could also match his appearance. Yes, he wanted something that could make him look cool.","Noah then looked toward the main cast.","The main protagonist Damien, just like any cliché hero, chose a sword. Despite already having one.","Kaelan, another important character, was holding two daggers and inspecting them carefully.","Lyria had taken a golden-colored spear that matched her appearance perfectly, especially with her blonde hair.","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly.","’I want something like that... a white-colored spear or maybe blue... damn, why is she so gorgeous?’","Noah’s eyes stayed glued to Lyria longer than necessary. It wasn’t his fault. He was a young man after all.","This was the same when Morgana had entered earlier.","Noah glanced back at her for a moment before turning forward again.","That woman looked even more breathtaking and seductive compared to the main heroines. It was understandable since a person’s appearance became better with each increase in the level of their mana core.","’Well, I’m already too handsome for my level. Even the protagonist can’t match me when it comes to appearance,’ Noah thought with a smirk as he ran his hand through his soft white hair.","He was really getting more narcissistic as time went on.","Then he saw another student.","Leonardo was confidently swinging a greatsword that was nearly the same length as his own height.","While Emma was wearing gauntlets.","Arisha was more of a magic spell user, but she also knew archery.","\"She’s also really beautiful,\" Noah muttered to himself, his eyes briefly drawn toward her chest area.","But only for a moment.","\"No! Focus!\"","He shook his head. ’What are you thinking, Noah! Go and get yourself a weapon.’","Forgetting to find a weapon for himself, he had started observing the main characters instead.","Noah walked to the other side.","After searching for a while, he finally found a spear to his liking.","He was really getting too picky.","He took the spear from the shelf.","The spear’s shaft was silver in color, while the pointed blade at the top was ocean blue, matching Noah’s eyes.","He placed his ID on the scanner and scanned it. The process only took a few seconds.","\"Alright, everything is done.\"","He swung the spear lightly a few times, then placed it inside his storage ring.","The students were still deciding which weapon to take. After all, there were just too many options there. Choosing one was really hard."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: First Day Training (1)","paragraphs":["After a while, almost every student had chosen their weapon.","Some held them proudly in their hands, testing their weight and balance, while others carefully stored them inside their storage rings.","Morgana, who had been silently observing from a distance, stepped forward. Her heels echoed softly against the metal floor.","Her violet eyes swept across the room, ensuring everyone was finished.","\"Since everyone has chosen their weapon,\" she said in a calm but authoritative tone, \"follow me.\"","Without waiting for a response, Morgana turned and walked toward the exit.","The students quickly followed behind her.","Noah also joined the group, walking quietly near the back of the crowd.","After walking through several corridors, they finally arrived at another enormous area. The moment the doors opened, the students were greeted by an even larger facility.","A massive training hall stretched before them. The hall itself was gigantic, but what surprised them even more was the enormous open training ground attached to it.","’Damn! This is huge!’ Noah was surprised again.","Many different practice areas were visible. Rows of practice weapon racks filled with training weapons were neatly arranged along the walls.","Large wooden dummies stood in several sections, designed for striking and combat drills.","There were dedicated shooting ranges for both archers and snipers.","Another section had moving targets that slid across rails. Some areas were divided into sparring platforms. Where students could spar against each other.","And on one side of the hall were several thick metallic doors with glowing panels beside them.","Students immediately began whispering again.","\"Whoa... this place is huge.\"","\"Look at those dummies.\"","\"Is that a shooting range?\"","\"What are those metal rooms over there?\"","Morgana stood before them and began explaining.","\"This is the primary training facility for first-year students.\"","Noah focused on what Morgana was saying.","She gestured toward the different sections. \"The areas with the wooden figures are for close combat training. The targets on the far side are for archery and projectile practice. The platforms in the middle are for sparring matches.\"","Then she pointed toward the metal doors. \"Those rooms are gravity chambers.\"","A ripple of surprise passed through the students.","\"Inside those rooms, the gravity can be increased beyond the normal level,\" Morgana continued calmly. \"They are used to strengthen your body and improve endurance.\"","Her sharp gaze moved across the group. \"However, most of you are not yet strong enough to handle high gravity levels.\"","Then she crossed her arms. \"Since today is the first day of the academy, I will not make you do anything heavy.\"","Some students visibly relaxed after hearing that. \"You may freely explore the training facility,\" Morgana continued. \"Use the equipment, practice with your weapon, or test the various sections.\"","Her tone became slightly colder. \"I will be observing all of you.\"","A faint pressure spread across the room. \"If any of you want advice or guidance, you may ask me.\"","With that, Morgana stepped aside. \"You may begin. Now go.\"","Immediately the students scattered in different directions.","Everyone was excited to test their abilities.","’Let’s go!’ Noah thought, but then he first observer others. What they were doing? Mostly main characters.","Damien Ashworth walked toward one of the open sparring platforms. He unsheathed his sword slowly. The blade gleamed faintly under the lights.","He took a calm stance and began practicing controlled sword movements, his strikes precise and disciplined.","Even without an opponent, his movements were clean and efficient. Several nearby students stopped to watch him.","Then Kaelan, he moved toward a quieter section near the combat dummies. He spun one of his daggers between his fingers before suddenly launching forward. His blades flashed as he struck the dummy multiple times in quick succession.","Thud! Thud! Thud!","Each strike landed with deadly accuracy. He moved around the dummy like a shadow.","’Ohh nice!’ Noah admired his footwork. Then turned his attention to others.","Lyria walked toward the open training ground outside the hall. She twirled her golden spear lightly before thrusting it forward in smooth motions.","’My Ly– no! not my! ...Lyria, her movements are better than mine for spear...lot better.’","Her movements were elegant and fluid. The spear cut through the air with sharp precision. Her blonde hair moved with each motion as she practiced.","While Emma headed toward the heavy training equipment. She tightened the gauntlets around her fists. Then she stepped in front of a reinforced dummy.","Boom!","Her punch slammed into the dummy with incredible force. The impact echoed through the area. Several nearby students turned to look at her in surprise.","’She got good physical strength’","Then Arisha, she calmly walked toward the archery range. She picked up a training bow and placed an arrow on the string. Her eyes focused on the distant target.","A moment later.","Thwip!","The arrow shot forward and struck the target directly near the center. She quietly prepared another shot.","’Where’s Leonardo?’ Then his blue eyes fell on the blonde hair man. ’There he is.’","Leonardo headed straight toward a large combat dummy. He rested the massive greatsword on his shoulder before lifting it with both hands. With a powerful shout, he swung it downward.","BANG!","The heavy blade slammed into the dummy. The ground beneath his feet shook slightly.","Noah stood keep standing near the entrance. His crystal blue eyes moved around the training hall as he observed all of them.","He watched the main characters spread out across the facility. ’Everyone already found their place,’ he thought.","He decided to stopped watching others. He then looked around the hall once more. Many students had gathered around the popular areas.","The sparring platforms were crowded. The archery range had several people waiting.","The dummies were surrounded by groups practicing together.","Noah scratched the back of his head. ’I don’t really want unnecessary attention. At least not yet.’","After scanning the hall, he noticed an empty corner near the far wall.","It was quiet. Almost no one was there. A faint smile appeared on his face.","’Perfect.’","Noah walked toward that corner. Once he reached it, he sat on the ground in cross leg position.","\"Alright,\" Noah muttered softly.","He closed his eyes and started to meditate for a while. Calm himself and circulate his mana.","Then he would practice his Ice Creation ability."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: First Day Training (2)","paragraphs":["After meditating for a while, Noah slowly exhaled.","He then slowly lifted his eyelids.","\"Okay... let’s try it again,\" he muttered quietly.","Mana started to circulate through his body faster. It flowed through his veins just like blood.","Slowly, it gathered around his extended arm. He condensed the mana into a thin rod of lightly compressed ice. It was dense and compact. He slowly shaped it like the shaft of a spear. Not extremely hard. He kept it slightly flexible and mobile.","The temperature around him dropped slightly. Frost formed beneath him where he was sitting.","After that came the spearhead. The place where there should be a blade.","He highly compressed the ice in that area. It became extremely dense. Slowly, he began shaping it into a spearhead, making it sharper with each layer of compression.","Soon, a spear was formed in his hand.","Noah held it firmly in his right hand. The touch was cold against his palm, yet it felt familiar.","Noah tightened his grip around the spear.","’Alright, now let’s train with this.’","He got up from his seat.","His left hand grasped the shaft near the upper side, while his right hand held the lower side.","He slowly exhaled.","Then he moved.","His left foot stepped forward while the spear he held horizontally shot out in a straight thrust.","The tip cut through the air with a soft whistle.","Noah pulled it back smoothly.","Another strike, this time slightly upward. If a person as tall as Noah had been standing there, it would have pierced their throat.","He performed simple and direct actions. There were no unnecessary movements.","Step forward.","Thrust.","He shifted his grip slightly and swept the spear sideways.","Slash.","This time he made a clean slash through the air.","Without pausing, Noah rotated the spear back and drove it forward again.","Thrust.","Then he pulled it back immediately.","Thrust.","His breathing remained calm and steady.","A drop of sweat slid down from his forehead, but his eyes remained focused on his practice.","Step forward.","Thrust.","Step back. Then in guard position.","Noah held the position for a moment before slowly lowering the weapon.","With a thoughtful expression, he murmured, \"Not bad... should I try this on a dummy?\"","He could feel it, the place where he was holding the shaft firmly had become wet.","The ice was slowly melting. Noah calmly channeled a bit of mana into it. Just like that, the melting stopped as the mana countered the temperature of the room and his body.","Then an indifferent yet strangely captivating voice came from behind him.","\"Is that ice spear created by you? Do you have the ability to create it?\"","The voice was familiar.","Noah immediately turned around.","Just a short distance away stood Morgana.","Now Noah could see her again from a close distance, and he couldn’t help but feel dazzled by her appearance.","The blazer suit could not hide her sinful curves. The soft-looking pair of peaks pressed against the outfit, giving them a perfectly round shape. Her waist was thin, but below it her hips widened, while her thighs looked thick beneath the skirt.","’Wish I could hold th—’","Noah quickly stopped himself from thinking further.","Straightening slightly, he replied respectfully, \"Instructor... yes. It’s related to my ability.\"","Morgana crossed her arms lightly and examined the spear with interest.","\"That’s quite a useful ability,\" she said thoughtfully. \"If I am not guessing wrong, you could create anything with ice... as long as you practice.\"","Noah respectfully bowed his head slightly.","\"Thank you, Instructor Morgana and yes I can create anything with ice.\"","Morgana raised one eyebrow slightly. She genuinely looked surprised by Noah’s attitude.","Noah noticed her expression.","’She must be shocked seeing a problem child like Noah behave so well. I am a well-behaved student after all.’","Noah smirked inwardly before straightening his posture.","\"Hm... not bad, Noah,\" Morgana said casually. \"I hope you will be like this all year. If you have doubts, you can consult with me.\"","A thought crossed her mind. Maybe he really had changed.","Noah nodded politely. \"Yes, Instructor. I will do that. Thanks again, Instructor.\"","At this point, Noah was acting like a disciplined student.","Morgana seemed satisfied with his attitude.","She turned around and walked in another direction, continuing to watch the other students train.","\"Oh... it seems I made a good impression on her after messing up in class.\"","’Good job, Noah!’ he thought while praising himself.","Noah then walked toward the area where the training dummies were placed.","He was going to practice with them for a while.","It was a big area. There were many dummies.","Noah walked toward the last one, away from Kaelan, Emma, and the others who were training.","He decided to use the same moves on the dummy that he had practiced a few minutes ago. His left foot stepped forward while the spear shot out in a straight thrust.","Thrust.","The tip of the spear whistled through the air before stopping precisely in front of the wooden dummy’s chest.","Noah pulled it back smoothly. Then he thrust again.","Thrust.","Another strike, this time aimed at the throat. His movements were not flashy.","There were no unnecessary spins or dramatic motions.","Every action was simple and direct. The spear moved like an extension of his body.","He shifted his grip slightly and swept the spear sideways.","Slash.","The wooden dummy rattled as the shaft struck its side.","Noah rotated the spear back and drove it forward again.","Thrust.","He attacked the dummy’s right shoulder.","Then pulled back. This time he thrust toward the left shoulder.","Thrust.","His breathing remained calm and steady.","A drop of sweat slid down the side of his face, but his eyes stayed focused on the dummy in front of him.","The spear stopped inches away from the dummy’s chest.","Perfectly controlled.","Noah held the position for a moment before slowly lowering the weapon.","Then he reset his stance and began again.","The voices of the students faded away behind him as Noah became completely focused on training.","His blue eyes were filled with slight excitement.","Each time he swung the spear, it felt easier, stronger, and more familiar."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: First trouble At Academy","paragraphs":["Finally, it was break time.","Since it was the first day of the academy, they didn’t teach many things. Just introductions.","Noah had noticed how the main characters were already becoming friends with each other.","He looked to his right. A few tables away from him, Damien, Emma, Leonard, Lyria, and Arisha were sitting together while eating their lunch.","Yes, they were currently in the cafeteria.","With a tired sigh, Noah muttered to himself, \"Hah... when will I make friends?\"","Munch.","He continued eating a chicken stick.","Though he was not someone who had many friends in his past life, he was still used to having a few friends around him every day in university, which kept him from getting bored.","But here he was alone. And if that was not enough, every time he tried to talk to someone, most of them ran away.","For lunch, there were many food items available.Roasted meat glazed with fragrant herbs. Bowls of butter-seared river fish. Golden honey bread that released warm steam when torn apart.","Students filled their plates with herb rice, grilled forest vegetables, and creamy mushroom stew.","Noah had nearly taken all of it.","There was no holding back when it came to free, tasty food.","The cafeteria itself was really huge, large enough for more than a thousand students to sit and eat at the same time.","’For now, I have to spend my time here like this.’","Noah continued eating, pushing those thoughts aside. For now, enjoying his meal came first.","---","Currently, Noah was walking through the hallway.","It was filled with students chatting loudly.","Here, no one noticed him or murmured about him, which was a very nice thing.","Noah could even see second-year and third-year students.","First-year students had red-colored ties and red-colored piping along the edges of their coats.","Second-years had black ones, while third-years had blue.","’What should I do now?’","He had no idea what to do other than train.","He didn’t have any future knowledge that could help him prepare for incoming dangers or obtain some cheat that was supposed to go to the main character.","’Why did I even get transmigrated? There’s no logic in this. If I don’t have future knowledge, then what change can I even bring to this world? Which idiot even transmigrated me here?’","Noah started cursing the person who had illogically transmigrated him.","Just then, someone approached from the opposite side of the hallway.","Murmurs followed as that person walked.","The reason was simple.","She was gorgeous.","Noah was pulled out of his thoughts after hearing students whisper about a beauty.","’A beautiful lady? Where is she? Who is it?’","Like a curious cat, Noah instantly tried to find her.","Only to suddenly stop walking. He stopped not because he was dazzled by her looks, but because he was surprised to see her again.","Walking toward him was a young woman with long, flowing dark-blue hair.","Her eyes were emerald green, like a lush forest.","Each step she took was filled with pride. She truly moved like a noble lady from a novel, carrying herself with elegance and grace.","Her figure was more on the slender side.","Her curves might have been slightly inferior to Lyria and Arisha, but they suited her perfectly.","She looked like a model.","’Fuck you, Noah! Why did you mess up when you had such an amazing fiancée?!’","He cursed the previous Noah again for doing something so foolish.","Click.","Click.","For some reason, Noah could clearly hear the clicking of her shoes against the floor.","Gulp.","Noah gulped down his saliva.","But then she stopped right in front of him. Just one hand’s distance separated them.","Her cold emerald eyes pierced into Noah’s blue ones.","Neither of them spoke for a while. Slowly, the attention of the surrounding students shifted toward Noah and Ophelia.","With a forced smile, Noah finally gathered the courage to speak.","\"Hm... hello?\" He tried to sound friendly.","Hearing his greeting, Ophelia frowned. Her eyes filled with clear disdain.","In a cold voice, she said, \"You really have no shame.\"","Noah blinked in confusion. Scratching his cheek slightly, he replied, \"Um... well, why is that?\"","He was shocked by her first words.","What shame was he supposed to feel? Because of what the old Noah had tried to do to her?","Yes, it was wrong. But it was not him who had done it.","And if that wasn’t enough, the real Noah had already been punished for it, being exiled from his family.","Though it was exile only in name. He was still known across the empire as the exiled, good-for-nothing son of the duke’s family.","Ophelia looked at him with disbelief. \"Wow. Look at you... asking why?\" she said sarcastically.","She closed her eyes and rubbed her temples as if trying to calm herself.","Then she glared at him again.","\"I can’t believe that after what you tried to do to me... you still have the courage to join this academy and show your face.\"","She sneered while looking at him with disgust.","Noah’s lips twitched slightly in irritation.","He did not feel sad.","Instead, he felt slightly annoyed.","Calmly, he replied, \"Hm... Ophelia, let’s not talk about the past.\"","Ophelia’s eyes turned colder. \"Yes... who would want to talk about the past,\" she said mockingly, \"when they have done something so lowly and disgusting?\"","She stared at him sharply.","\"I am really surprised by your audacity... to stand in front of me like what you did was nothing.\"","Meanwhile, whispers began spreading among the students nearby.","\"I remember now. That handsome boy... Noah Eldritch.\"","\"Oh... did he do something? I heard he was exiled, but I don’t know the reason.\"","\"Well, I heard it was something really disgusting.\"","\"But those might just be rumors.\"","Students started gossiping while watching the drama unfold. Noah ignored their comments. He just wanted to leave.","But still he remained. Actually he was even preparing to talk with her in future. It’s true that his someone else. But what old Noah did was really wrong. Even though he shouldn’t feel this way, somewhere in his heart he still felt guilty.","Also he don’t want any more trouble at academy from her.","So Noah did what needed to do.","He bow to her in 90 degree angle.","\"Ophelia...I am truly sorry for what I have done to you. I am ashamed of my actions. I know what I did was not something that any woman could ever forgive. And I don’t expect this from you either. But I still wanted to tell you I am really sorry for that.\""]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Causing Trouble On First Day (1)","paragraphs":["\"What?!\" Ophelia flinched at his sudden action.","Noah was bowing to her and apologizing. It looked too sincere. His voice sounded honest.","\"Oh my? What’s going on?\"","\"He’s bowing? Is he apologizing to her?\"","\"She was his fiancée. Yet what he did was shameful. Now asking for forgiveness won’t change anything.\"","Murmurs followed.","Ophelia clenched her fists. Her eyes were filled with shock.","What was happening?","She couldn’t understand it.","She had known Noah for years. An arrogant boy who did whatever he wanted. A wasted young man with no future. Someone who never felt guilty for his actions.","And now the same boy was bowing to her, saying sorry.","That was not the Noah she knew. Now it was her who was baffled by the situation. But then she shook her head.","What Noah had done was not something forgivable. With a cold expression, she spoke sharply.","\"So now you are shamelessly asking for forgiveness... after trying such things. Do you think your apology would change anything?\"","Noah straightened his back. Calmly, he replied, \"No, I know it won’t. And I’m not asking you to forgive me. But I still wanted to say this.\"","Ophelia went silent. Her eyes trembled for a few seconds before calming down again. She looked at him with the same cold indifference.","\"I will never forgive you, Noah...\" She paused for a while, then said, \"You really are a pathetic man.\"","Ophelia’s last words made him slightly angry.","’Control yourself, Noah! She has every right to be angry with you... but damn!’ He knew her anger was understandable and that she was not wrong.","But it still irritated him. Slowly, the guilt inside him faded away.","’Since I apologized to her... and she’s still angry... a little teasing won’t matter much. I mean, she already hates me so much... she’ll just hate me more. Nothing much.’","After making these wrong excuses to himself and convincing himself that what he was about to do wasn’t wrong...","He stared at her. A wide smile slowly appeared on his face. His eyes looked gentle. He leaned slightly closer to her.","’I am really going to be in big trouble... but fuck it, I don’t care! I can’t stop myself.’","Softly, he said,","\"Ophelia... let me make up for what I did. How about you do the same thing to me that I tried to do to you? I won’t fight back. Then we’ll be even... and there won’t be any reason to hate me.\"","\"WHAT?!\"","Ophelia stepped back with wide eyes. She was beyond shocked. Her cheeks turned faintly pink. It was hard to tell why. Was it embarrassment? Or pure anger? Or perhaps she was imagining the scenario where she tried to do the same thing to him?","It could have been anything. But Noah didn’t care. He was more satisfied by her reaction. ’Get more angry. I’ll feel more satisfied.’","For some reason, he wanted to see her even more annoyed.","Her face flushed slightly with anger. \"You shameless bastard!\" she shouted.","\"How dare you think I would do so—something s-so disgusting and lowly?!\"","Her voice was louder this time. Other students could clearly hear her now.","And she noticed it. Her eyes quickly darted around as she realized many students were watching them.","Clicking her tongue in irritation, she glared at Noah one last time. \"Tch! Don’t talk to me again. Stay away from me while we are in this academy.\"","With that, she turned around and walked away. Leaving Noah standing there.","And Noah... He felt strangely satisfied.","With a grin, he muttered to himself, \"Haha... that was fun.\"","Then his face turned calm. \"...Did I do the right thing? Damn... I think I shouldn’t have done that.\" After thinking for a while, he started to feel bad.","\"Anyways..\"","Then he looked around. Everyone was staring at him.","Noah frowned at their gazes. \"What are you looking at?!\" he snapped angrily.","\"Was there a show going on here?! Scram off!\" His expression was clearly irritated.","He had just acted like some delinquent student threatening or ordering normal students.","The surrounding students flinched at his words and quickly started moving away.","They didn’t want to mess with someone like Noah.","Who knew what kind of madness this troublesome, exiled son might do?","It was better not to get involved with him.","\"Good,\" he nodded.","He adjusted his tie like some professional businessman.","Then he started to walk.","But his trouble was not over yet.","\"Oh my~ Look here... It’s the first day, and the young mast—oh sorry, I mean the exiled young master of the Eldritch family is already making trouble.\"","A mocking voice came from behind.","Noah stopped in his tracks. Then he turned back to see who had come to annoy him. Standing there were three young men of his age.","Their uniforms indicated they were first-year students. In the middle stood a man with dark brown hair and hazel eyes. He was as tall as Noah and was looking at him with a mocking smile.","On his right side stood a man with round glasses on his nose and black hair. He was giving Noah a knowing smile.","On the left side stood a slightly fat man with dirty blonde hair. He was smiling widely.","Noah looked at the trio with amusement. \"Who are you guys? Do I know you?\" Noah asked, still slightly annoyed.","\"What?! Di–Did you ask who we are?\" the fat boy spoke in bewilderment. The brown-haired guy gritted his teeth but still maintained his smile.","Meanwhile, the glasses-wearing man stopped smiling.","He raised his index finger and pushed the bridge of his glasses.","For a second, his glasses reflected the light.","\"Now you are acting like you don’t know us... You really have no shame,\" the brown-haired guy said with irritation, though his smile never disappeared.","’Maybe I know them... They look familiar.’","Noah forced himself to search through the real Noah’s memories.","After thinking for a while, he finally remembered them.","\"Edward, it’s you!\" he said, looking at the brown-haired man.","Then he looked at the fat one. \"And you are Richard.\"","Then he turned toward the black-haired guy. \"And you... you are Glasses-kun... wait, I mean Tetsu Sugiyama. Or should I say your surname first, Sugiyama Tetsu?\"","\"Don’t you dare call me Glasses-kun!\" Tetsu warned Noah with an annoyed face.","\"Oh, it seems you got your memory back pretty fast,\" Edward said as the trio walked toward him.","Noah remained standing there with both his hands inside the pockets of his trousers."]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Causing Trouble On First Day (2)","paragraphs":["’They are not going to let this chance go away.’","Noah thought while looking at the trio. He knew them; they were like his underlings... only during family gatherings.","Edward was from the Count Beaufort family, while the other two were from viscount families. During family gatherings, they always acted like his underlings, while Noah acted arrogant and like someone who was above them.","’Damn, I have treated them a little badly in the past.’","Though he wasn’t used to meeting them much, every time he met them, he acted like their master. No wonder they were going to get back at him since he was now an exiled son.","Also, in the academy, where background rarely matters.","Of course, being from a ducal family does have some power that he could have used, but well... he was exiled.","\"So what just happened? You bowed to your ex-fiancée and even got insulted by her... in front of so many! Well, you kind of deserved it! Hahah!\"","\"Haha,\" Glasses-kun also joined his laughter.","\"I can’t help but enjoy that scene, the arrogant Noah bowing and getting insulted! Haha!\" The fat boy laughed while mocking him.","’Oh, is this... my face-slapping moment? ...But I don’t want to cause more trouble for today.’ Noah didn’t react... or at least he tried. A vein had already bulged on his forehead.","Firstly, he got insulted by Ophelia. He didn’t mind much since he had done something wrong. Even if he was not the real one, he was still in that body.","But now this trio was mocking him openly. How could he remain silent?","\"Haha, what? Are you angry?\" Edward leaned forward with a mocking expression as he continued.","\"He must want to cry!\" Glasses-kun said.","\"Maybe he wants to run to his mama and complain to her.\"","\"Wait, but his mama kicked him out of the house and the family.\"","The trio went silent and then laughed loudly. They were talking in a loud voice, so a few students who still remained nearby could hear them.","’Hah... I guess that’s enough.’ Noah didn’t say anything. At this moment, he needed to control himself.","He took out his mobile and opened the app that belonged to the academy. Noah immediately opened the academy website and went through the guidelines to see what action he could take against these third-rate bullies.","\"Hm? What are you doing? Calling someone?\" Edward stopped laughing and saw Noah. He leaned closer to see what he was searching for, then looked at his face. \"Give up. No one will help a pathetic man like you. A loser should just know their place and stay silent.\"","Noah’s fingers tightened around his mobile as he scrolled through the guidelines.","’Calm down, Noah! Calm down.’","\"Hahaha! Oh, he must be scared of us.\" Testu mock him further.","\"Hope he won’t pee in his pants right here.\" Richard also had no wish to step back.","Just then Noah’s eyes fell on one line.","’Oh... this is good.’","Noah put his mobile in his storage ring and looked up at the trio with a kind, gentle smile.","Which actually made the trio confused.","\"Did you hit your brain? Why are you smiling?\" Tetsu asked with a knowing smile.","\"Should we knock some sense into him?\" Richard said while punching his palm with the fist of his other hand.","Edward glanced sideways. \"Not a bad idea. But beating a loser does feel lowly.\" An evil smile formed on his face.","He turned back to see Noah, but what came into his view was a fist. Yes, a real fist. Before he could react, it hit his cheek.","It was a powerful punch that Noah threw at Edward. He wanted to punch his nose, but it might have been too much, so he chose his cheek.","The punch was powerful enough to send Edward to the ground. He fell and sat on his rear.","\"Arrghh!\" A painful groan left him.","Thud!","\"What the hell?!\"","\"Hey!\"","Both Richard and Tetsu were shocked and screamed.","Noah didn’t wait for them to react. His right foot moved in front of Richard. Then his left fist shot forward with sudden speed.","Richard’s eyes widened. \"Wai—?!\"","Before he could finish speaking.","BOOM!","The punch slammed directly into his round belly.","\"Gahh!\"","Richard doubled over instantly, clutching his stomach as the air was knocked out of his lungs.","Tetsu stared at the scene in disbelief. \"You—!\"","But Noah had already moved again.","Students around them gasped and quickly stepped away, creating space in the hallway. No one wanted to get caught in the fight.","Edward groaned as he pushed himself up from the ground. His eyes burned with anger.","\"You bastard!\"","Richard also recovered slightly, breathing heavily.","Tetsu’s expression turned serious.","The three of them quickly surrounded Noah. Edward wiped the corner of his mouth.","\"You think you can attack us and walk away?\"","Richard cracked his knuckles again. \"We’ll beat the crap out of you!\"","The three of them rushed forward. Edward threw the first punch.","Noah tilted his head slightly and dodged it.","Richard tried to grab Noah from the side. Noah pushed him away with his shoulder.","Tetsu lunged forward with a fast strike.","Noah was fighting them alone. He ducked down and avoided Tetsu’s punch.","But then another fist came at him from the other side. It was from Richard. Noah took the hit on his hand by covering his face.","But Edward was successful in hitting his cheek from the front.","Bam!","\"Take this, bastard!\"","Noah’s head was thrown back. He could taste his blood. But that wouldn’t stop him.","He moved again. His right foot moved forward as he kicked Richard’s knee.","\"Arggh!\"","Just then a punch from Tetsu hit against his lower ribs.","\"Fuck!\"","Soon the fight turned chaotic. Fists clashed against each other. Bodies collided.","The trio began using mana. A faint glow appeared around their bodies as they reinforced their strength.","Edward’s fist came flying toward Noah again.","Noah quickly raised his hands.","Cold mana surged through his arms.","Crack.","Ice formed instantly around both his fists. A pair of icy gauntlets wrapped around his fists.","The transparent ice hardened, covering his knuckles like armor.","Noah clenched his fists. The icy gauntlets gleamed faintly.","\"Come on,\" Noah declaired with a wide smile. He was actually enjoying beating them.","The fight in the corridor continued as students hurriedly backed away from the scene."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: Causing Trouble On First Day (3)","paragraphs":["Mana exploded from Noah’s body. Both his fists collided against each other, making a loud sound.","BAM!","While trying many things with his Ice Creation ability over the past few days, he had also tried forming gauntlets. They were much easier to create compared to a sword or spear. Also, for some reason, he could handle the coldness against his skin without any problem.","The trio summoned their weapons.","Tetsu was holding a bow with an arrow on its string. Edward held a greatsword, while Richard had a spear. Mana trembled around the three of them.","Oddly, Noah didn’t feel any fear. Instead, he felt slightly angry and wanted to beat the three of them.","\"Come at me!\"","Noah kicked off the ground and dashed forward. He lunged into the air toward the trio. With a crazed grin, he lifted his fist at Edward. Edward stepped back instantly.","BOOM!","Noah’s fist struck the floor, and a crack formed on the ground from the impact.","Noah didn’t waste time and quickly looked up.","The trio hadn’t attacked him. For some reason, they hadn’t reacted to him at all.","They were surprised and looking straight. No... not straight. They were looking past Noah.","Now his expression turned confused. Before he could think further, a strong force collided with him from behind.","\"Gah!\"","Pain shot through his back from the impact. Noah immediately fell to the floor on his front.","THUD!","Instantly, someone grabbed both his hands from behind and locked them together against his back with a strong grip.","He was pressed down by someone, his right cheek pushed against the cold floor.","He could feel the weight of someone on his body.","\"First day... and already causing trouble at the academy. You juniors are really something.\"","A feminine voice came from behind rather, from above Noah.","\"Se-Senior... it’s not what you think! This guy was the first one to attack us,\" Edward defended himself the moment he saw the senior intervene.","\"Yes, he’s right. We are innocent here.\"","\"We are not wrong.\"","Noah understood the situation.","’Damn! Why am I the one getting subdued? I am alone while they are three.’","\"It doesn’t matter who started it. You all fought, so you are all responsible for the mess you created here. Now follow me quietly!\"","The trio put their weapons back into their storage rings.","\"Yes, Ma’am!\"","\"Yes, Ma’am!\"","\"Yes, Ma’am!\"","They answered in unison.","Noah also dismissed his ice gauntlets. Cracks appeared on them, and soon they shattered into tiny ice particles.","Seeing that, the woman who had subdued him finally released her grip.","Noah immediately felt lighter, realizing the heavy weight on his body was gone.","He pushed himself up and finally saw the person who had done this to him.","He was surprised.","She was a young woman, around 164 cm tall. Her frame leaned toward the petite side.","Yet the force Noah had felt from her was terrifying. He couldn’t even move when she had subdued him.","She had medium-length brown hair and eyes of the same color.","She was looking at him with cold eyes, her hands folded under her chest.","\"Let’s go.\"","Noah didn’t say anything and followed her.","The trio followed behind them.","---","Inside the cabin of Instructor Morgana Celestine.","Five students were standing in front of her desk.","One of them was wearing a second-year uniform, showing that she was a second-year student.","The other four were first-year students.","The four young men’s uniforms were messy.","Edward had a bruise on his left cheek, as if someone had punched him hard.","Richard was holding his belly with a slightly painful expression.","Meanwhile, Tetsu kept shaking his leg from time to time as if it was hurting. He was trying to adjust to the pain.","The fourth student was a handsome young man she recognized.","He had a bruise on his cheek, though not as severe as Edward’s. Despite that, he was standing normally.","Morgana knew this young man.","He was a student in her class. Someone she had spoken to just an hour ago during training.","On Noah’s side, he remained calm on the outside.","But inside, he was anything but calm.","’Dammit... everything is a mess. I thought I had made a good impression on the instructor during training... but now it’s ruined again.’","He glanced at the senior who had brought him here.","She had a badge of the Discipline Committee, which operated under the Student Council. A large unit responsible for handling fights in the academy, rule violations, and similar matters.","Noah wondered why this woman had brought him to Morgana instead of taking them directly to the leader of the Discipline Committee.","\"According to these three students, Noah attacked them first. And he is your student, Instructor Morgana. Usually I would have taken them to the council, but since it’s the first day, I thought it would be better to bring them to you. This way, you can handle the matter involving your own student rather than them being punished by the council on the first day.\"","Morgana nodded.","\"It’s good that you did that, Ria.\"","\"Instructor Morgana, don’t let Noah get away with this! Look at what he has done. He beat us without thinking at all. Fighting is not allowed in the academy unless it’s a spar or an official challenge. Yet he attacked us—\"","Morgana raised her hand, stopping him before he could continue.","\"I get it.\"","Her violet eyes shifted toward Noah.","\"Noah Eldritch... don’t you know that fighting on campus is prohibited? Haven’t you read the guidelines?\"","Noah nodded.","\"Yes. I read them.\"","\"Then why did you do this?\"","\"...Well, they were mocking me... insulting me... so I checked what action I could take against them. At that time, I saw a rule stating that if a fight breaks out on campus, the student who started it will receive punishment. If it’s the first offense, only a certain number of credit points are deducted. Nothing serious.\"","Noah looked to the side, avoiding her dangerous gaze.","\"So... I thought losing a few credit points wasn’t a big deal. So I beat them.\"","When he finished speaking, everyone in the room looked at him in surprise.","Even Morgana seemed slightly stunned by his reasoning."]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Mary","paragraphs":["She rubbed her temples.","\"Hah... I thought you had changed... but I guess I was wrong.\"","She glared directly into his eyes.","\"Fifty credit points will be deducted from you. Also, after lectures end today, you will clean all the washrooms on the floor of your classroom.\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","Meanwhile, the trio smirked with delight. Even Ria was shocked by the punishment.","If she had taken him to the Discipline Committee, he wouldn’t have been forced to clean washrooms.","But well... he had received extra punishment. Noah looked at her with eyes as if this was some kind of injustice.","He didn’t mind getting punished. But... With a dissatisfied expression, he spoke.","\"What about them? They also fought back. They even insulted me!\"","Morgana looked at him calmly, then replied with a cold expression.","\"Hah... in that case it was self-defense. Also, those three look more hurt compared to you. And even if they insulted you... you could have used another way. Soon you guys could challenge each other for sparring. You could have done that... and taken your anger out on them.\"","Then she looked at him with a stern gaze.","\"But no... you just tried to beat them like a delinquent student.\"","Then she turned her gaze toward Edward and the others.","With a warning look, she said,","\"Also, you three... don’t bother my student again or go around insulting others. If I find out about it next time... you won’t leave without punishment like today.\"","\"\"\"Yes Ma’am!\"\"\" the trio replied again in unison.","\"Tch!\" Noah clicked his tongue in annoyance.","Ria simply shook her head tiredly.","\"Now you guys are dismissed. Go away!\" Morgana said with an irritated voice.","Noah didn’t wait and immediately left the cabin, followed by the trio.","Only Ria and Morgana remained inside the cabin.","Ria crossed her arms and spoke with a slightly worried smile.","\"Instructor Morgana... you really got a troublesome student. Noah Eldritch is known for that, after all.\"","Morgana shook her head slowly, then sighed.","\"I don’t think so... well, I hope he won’t...\"","Then her expression turned firm.","\"...but if he continues to cause trouble, I will be sure to teach him a lesson. Under my instruction, he will change for sure.\"","This time her expression was full of confidence.","Ria raised her brow in amusement.","\"If you say so, Instructor Morgana.\"","Then she bowed slightly.","\"Well, I will go now.\"","She left the cabin, leaving Morgana alone inside.","---","Since it was the first day, there were not many lectures.","Though Morgana was the head instructor of their class, it didn’t mean she taught everything. A few classes were handled by other instructors.","Subjects such as alchemy, history, and mana theory were taught by different instructors.","Currently, Noah was inside a washroom, cleaning its floor with a broom.","With an annoyed expression, he muttered,","\"Tch! This world is so advanced and has so many types of magic. Yet they gave me a broom to clean this shit!\"","He was still annoyed about what had happened today.","He didn’t visit the infirmary since he had hardly received any strong hits or serious wounds.","\"Hmm~ hm~\" Noah started humming while cleaning.","Nothing would change even after complaining now.","’There are so many beautiful girls here. My friends always used to tease me for being single in university... Though I never wished to be in a relationship. But man, seeing such beautiful ladies sure makes my heart beat faster and makes me want to have one.’","Once again, he was thinking about nonsense things.","Rather than thinking about survival in this world, he was wondering whether getting into a relationship was a good idea or not.","’Then there’s Ophelia...another big problem...’","He stopped sweeping as he thought of her. But not for long. With an indifferent shrug, he muttered,","\"Meh... I will see how it goes with her.\"","After a while, the last washroom was finally cleaned. He picked up the broom and the bucket of water.","He stepped out of the washroom. Only to collide with someone.","\"What?!\" Noah exclaimed in surprise.","What came into his view was short, neck-length black hair.","\"Sorry!\" the person who had bumped into him quickly said.","It was a woman. She hadn’t been moving too fast, so neither of them fell. She stepped back slightly and bowed while apologizing.","She wore large round glasses over her black eyes.","Her features were normal.","She had a delicate, cute nose. Below it were soft, plump rosy lips. Her skin was smooth and fair.","Her figure was slender, with a cute face. Her height was around 167 cm. She was not as beautiful as the female leads of the game, but she was still cute.","Noah remained silent for a moment, then nodded calmly.","\"No worries. You were not at fault.\"","She nodded, but then looked at him with slight confusion.","Noah noticed her expression.","\"Is there something you want to talk about?\" he asked.","She hesitated for a moment, then spoke cautiously. \"Why did you come out of the... female washroom?\"","Noah blinked.","He immediately understood why she looked confused... or maybe suspicious.","He raised the broom slightly and showed it to her.","\"Can you see this? I was cleaning the washroom.\"","Then he turned around and showed her the sign hanging on the door that read Closed for Cleaning.","But hearing him only made her look even more confused.","With a puzzled expression, she said,","\"But why were you cleaning it? Isn’t there staff for doing this? Also, they have better machines which help them clean it easily instead of using a broom.\"","Hearing that only made Noah more irritated.","His lips twitched.","’It seems the news about me getting punished on the first day didn’t spread... well, I guess it’s not that big of a deal to spread like rumors. Nor am I some big shot.’","Looking at her face, he forced a gentle smile.","\"Well... I was punished by Instructor Morgana.\"","Her eyes widened in surprise.","\"So that’s why you are here. What did you do to get punished?\"","Noah scratched his cheek awkwardly and smiled worriedly.","\"I kind of... fought against three students from another class.\"","Her expression immediately turned serious.","\"Why did you do that? Don’t you know it’s wrong to fight unofficially, especially on campus?\"","Noah shrugged casually.","\"They insulted me... so I got angry and did it. Haha.\"","He chuckled awkwardly at his own words.","She sighed with a slightly disapproving look.","\"You are already causing trouble on the first day.\"","Noah simply replied with a helpless expression.","\"As I said, they mocked me and insulted me. So that’s why I did that.\"","She raised her hands slightly as if ending the topic.","\"Okay, okay! Let it go now. Don’t fight again. By the way, what’s your name?\"","Noah answered calmly.","\"...It’s Noah.\"","Her eyes widened again.","\"You... You are Noah Eldritch?\"","Noah looked at her curiously.","\"Yeah, I am. Is there any problem with that? And what’s your name?\"","She quickly waved her hands and shook her head nervously.","\"No! No! There’s none. Haha... I am Mary.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Ohh... I heard your name during attendance. No wonder I felt like I had seen you somewhere.\"","She scratched her cheek awkwardly.","\"Yeah... in my case, I didn’t pay attention to other students... so I didn’t know you were Noah. I will go to the washroom now. Bye!\"","She quickly walked past Noah and entered the washroom.","Noah looked at the door with a puzzled expression.","\"...Why did she look nervous after hearing my name?\"","He already knew the answer.","\"Whatever...\"","He walked through the hallway to return the broom.","---","It was already evening.","Noah was late because of the cleaning punishment.","Now it was time for him to return to his dormitory room.","He had wanted to train for a while, but that time had been wasted on cleaning.","While walking through the campus toward the dormitory building area, Noah noticed someone walking ahead of him.","’Damien...also...Leonard and others.’","It was the protagonist of the game. While beside him were Leonard, Emma and Lyria.","Noah stared at his back for a few seconds. Just when he was about to look away. Damien suddenly turned back.His eyes met Noah’s directly."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Nova Points","paragraphs":["The hazel eyes of the young man met the ocean-blue eyes of Noah. Damien had stopped walking, staring back at him.","Noah didn’t know how to react to his sudden stare, but he remained calm on the outside, giving a gentle smile with his handsome face.","Leonard, Emma, and Lyria stopped walking after noticing Damien had suddenly halted.","With a slightly confused expression, Emma raised a brow.","\"What happened, Damien?\"","Her eyes followed Damien’s gaze. She saw Noah standing a few meters away from them.","With curiosity in her eyes, Lyria glanced at Noah.","\"Do you know Noah?\" she asked from beside him.","With surprise clearly visible on his face, Leonard spoke.","\"You really know him?!\"","He clearly knew who Noah was; after all, they had met before at some family gathering.","And even Noah remembered that this guy, Leonard, didn’t like him.","With a calm expression, Damien shook his head slightly.","\"It’s nothing... I just felt something... I guess it was just my imagination. Let’s go.\"","He turned forward and resumed walking.","The group began moving together again.","With a warning tone, Leonardo looked at Damien.","\"Hey, don’t try to get closer to that guy, Noah.\"","With a serious expression, Emma added,","\"Yeah. I’ve heard some rumors about him, and all of them were bad.\"","With a gentle expression, Lyria spoke softly,","\"Hey, you shouldn’t say such things about others if you’re not sure.\"","’Fuck! I can hear you clearly!’ Noah thought while standing there.","He let them move farther away before he started walking again.","With a faint smile, he muttered under his breath,","\"Lyria is such a kind soul.\"","If he had played the game, he was sure she would have been one of his favorite characters.","Noah then looked at Damien. ’That guy just sense a gaze directed at him...his crazy!’","---","Two days later.","In the classroom, Noah sat calmly on the back bench while listening to the lecture. Instructor Morgana was teaching.","Her loud voice resounded throughout the classroom.","Instructor Morgana stood at the front, her sharp violet eyes sweeping across the students.","\"As you might already know, monsters—also called mana beasts are divided into ranks from F to SS. They possess a mana core inside their bodies, mostly near their heart. As I already told you yesterday, they are helpful for you to absorb mana from and level up.\"","Noah listened carefully.","On the first day, she didn’t teach anything. On the second day, she mostly taught about the power system, how to meditate and circulate mana properly. On the third day, she mostly taught about basic survival things. What one should do if they stuck in unknown place. And many others.","Now she was explaining this monster rankings.","Since she was the head instructor, her duty was to guide the class as well as possible. So she taught even small things from time to time.","Which was a good thing.","Well, not many lectures had been conducted in the last three days since they were allowing students to get accustomed to the academy. Its surroundings, rules, and regulations.","But Morgana had made them train for hours since lectures from other instructors hadn’t started yet.","Taking them to the training facility, she would force all students to train.","And if she caught someone slacking, they were doomed to hear her scolding.","\"Each rank has three stages. F-, F, and F+. The same system applies to all ranks up to SS. F rank monster is similar level in strength compare to Dormant core perosn. While minus, neutral and plus stages of them are similar to low, mid and high of each core stages,\" she continued, her violet eyes surveying all the students.","\"Just like that an SS rank monster is on same level that of Sovereign Core level individual. They posses enough strength to destroy cities alone.\"","Her voice brought Noah’s attention fully back to the lecture.","\"Now let us stop here for today’s lecture. I need to tell you something important.\"","She tapped the board lightly with her staff.","\"Listen carefully. What I’m about to explain is something that will directly affect your life inside and outside the academy.\"","A few students straightened up immediately.","Even Noah, sitting at the back, shifted his attention fully toward her.","Morgana continued, her voice calm but authoritative.","\"Novaris Academy is not just an institution for education. It governs the entire city of Novaris. Every shop, facility, training ground, and even certain restricted zones... all fall under the academy’s authority. Most of you already know this.\"","A faint ripple of surprise spread through the class.","It was general knowledge. Many knew it, while many didn’t.","Morgana smirked slightly.","\"Yes. Which means your performance here doesn’t just decide your grades, it decides your status.\"","She turned and wrote two words on the board.","Nova Points","\"These,\" she said, tapping the words, \"are your lifeline.\"","\"Every student receives a fixed amount of Nova Points at the start of each month. Nova is simply the short form of Novaris.\"","Emma raised her hand slightly.","\"What can we use them for?\"","Morgana glanced at her and replied calmly,","\"These will be used just like money. As I have instructed before, I hope you have already downloaded the academy app. It contains all academy information rules, regulations, ranks, and your ID information. Notifications for important things.You just have to log in with your ID number. There, you can see your Nova Points and use them.\"","She began pacing slowly.","\"You can use Nova Points across the city cafés, equipment stores, training arenas, private rooms, even certain premium services that you might think are only possible with money. They can be bought with normal currency as well.\"","She paused, letting it sink in.","\"Of course, your regular currency Zela—still exists. But Nova Points...\" her lips curled slightly, \"...will act as a replacement for you in place of money.\"","Now the class was fully hooked.","Lyria tilted her head slightly.","\"So... everyone gets the same amount?\"","Morgana chuckled softly.","\"If only the world were that fair.\"","She turned back to the class.","\"Your monthly Nova Points are influenced by your rank. You all get the same base amount, that’s true, but...\"","A wave of tension spread instantly.","\"...students within the Top 50 receive bonus points.\"","Murmurs broke out.","\"And those within the Top 10...\" her voice lowered slightly, \"...receive significantly higher rewards.\"","Leonardo’s eyes sharpened.","\"Moreover,\" Morgana added, \"the higher your rank, the greater your monthly allocation becomes. The difference between Rank 50 and Rank 1...\" she paused, \"...is not small.\"","Noah leaned back slightly, listening quietly.","Morgana’s gaze hardened.","\"This system exists for one reason.\"","She struck the board once.","\"To create competition.\"","Silence.","\"No charity. No equality. Only results.\" Her eyes scanned the room once more.","\"If you want better resources, better opportunities, better treatment...\"","A faint, cold smile appeared on her face. \"Then climb.\"","No one spoke. Even the air felt heavier.","At the back, Noah rested his chin on his hand.","\"...Now this,\" he muttered under his breath, \"...is real shit.\"","He took out his mobile and opened the app.","There, he could see his information on his profile.","His eyes widened slightly.","\"You can check your apps. This morning you might have received your points in your account,\" Morgana added.","Noah looked at the number.","\"1,00,000 is the basic points... then how much do they give to Rank One...\" he muttered in amusement.","The class was once again filled with murmurs and chatter as students checked their points."]}]);
